window.PYQ_OCR['rrb-para'].push({t:'rrb para 2025 04 29 shift 2',q:[{"n": 1, "q": "When an object is placed between the pole and the focus of a concave mirror, what is the position of the image? Ans 1. Behind the mirror 2. Cannot be determined 3. In front of the mirror 4. On the mirror Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100995523 Option 1 ID : 441009380050 Option 2 ID : 441009380051 Option 3 ID : 441009380049 Option 4 ID : 441009380048 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 2, "q": "Which of the following pairs correctly lists examples of Maharatna and Navratna companies in India? Ans 1. Maharatna: Indian Oil Corporation Limited; Navratna: Bharat Electronics Limited 2. Maharatna: Bharat Sanchar Nigam Limited; Navratna: Indian Railway Catering and Tourism Corporation Limited 3. Maharatna: Hindustan Aeronautics Limited; Navratna: Steel Authority of India Limited 4. Maharatna: Airport Authority of India; Navratna: Mahanagar Telephone Nigam Limited Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100995732 Option 1 ID : 441009380898 Option 2 ID : 441009380897 Option 3 ID : 441009380899 Option 4 ID : 441009380896 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 3, "q": "In a certain code language, ‘MAKE’ is coded as ‘6413’ and ‘PEAK’ is coded as ‘4176’. What is the code for ‘M’ in the given code language? Ans 1. 6 2. 1 3. 3 4. 4 Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009170427 Option 1 ID : 441009674622 Option 2 ID : 441009674624 Option 3 ID : 441009674621 Option 4 ID : 441009674623 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 4, "q": "Based on the English alphabetical order, three of the following four letter-clusters are alike in a certain way and thus form a group. Which letter-cluster DOES NOT belong to that group? (Note: The odd one out is not based on the number of consonants/vowels or their position in the letter-cluster.) Ans 1. LJI 2. XVU 3. TRQ 4. QPN Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009170397 Option 1 ID : 441009674501 Option 2 ID : 441009674504 Option 3 ID : 441009674503 Option 4 ID : 441009674502 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 5, "q": "In 2025, which major technology company announced a $3 billion investment to enhance its cloud and AI infrastructure in India, including plans to train 10 million locals in AI skills by 2030? Ans 1. Google 2. IBM 3. Microsoft 4. Amazon Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100977956 Option 1 ID : 441009309826 Option 2 ID : 441009309829 Option 3 ID : 441009309827 Option 4 ID : 441009309828 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 6, "q": "BUOP is related to FYST in a certain way based on the English alphabetical order. In the same way, RKEF is related to VOIJ. To which of the following options is DWQR related, following the same logic? Ans 1. HUYT 2. HAUV 3. HVUA 4. HAVU Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009170419 Option 1 ID : 441009674592 Option 2 ID : 441009674589 Option 3 ID : 441009674591 Option 4 ID : 441009674590 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 7, "q": "Each of L, M, N, O, W, X and Y has an exam on a different day of a week starting from Monday and ending on Sunday of the same week. Y has exam on Thursday. W has exam before Y and only one person has exam between them. Only four people have exams between N and W. M has exam on one of the days after W. X has exam on the day immediately before L. How many people have exam between L and M? Ans 1. Two 2. One 3. Three 4. Four Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009170404 Option 1 ID : 441009674530 Option 2 ID : 441009674529 Option 3 ID : 441009674531 Option 4 ID : 441009674532 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 8, "q": "A scientist conducts an experiment by heating 50 g of mercury(II) oxide in a closed container. After heating, it decomposes into mercury and oxygen gas. What will be the total mass of the products? Ans 1. Less than 50 g because mercury(II) oxide decomposes. 2. More than 50 g because oxygen gas is released. 3. Exactly 50 g because mass is conserved. 4. Cannot be determined without knowing oxygen’s mass. Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100971250 Option 1 ID : 441009283392 Option 2 ID : 441009283391 Option 3 ID : 441009283393 Option 4 ID : 441009283394 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 9, "q": "Who among the following was the leader of the Wahabi Movement in India that started in the first half of the 19th century? Ans 1. Shah Waliullah 2. Maulana Abul Kalam Azad 3. Syed Ahmed Barelvi 4. Abdul Wahab Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100984047 Option 1 ID : 441009333923 Option 2 ID : 441009333920 Option 3 ID : 441009333922 Option 4 ID : 441009333921 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 10, "q": "126 is related to 181 following a certain logic. Following the same logic, 89 is related to 144. To which of the given options is 130 related, following the same logic? (Note: Operations should be performed on the whole numbers, without breaking down the numbers into their constituent digits. E.g., 13 – Operations on 13 such as adding/subtracting/multiplying to 13 can be performed. Breaking down 13 into 1 and 3 and then performing mathematical operations on 1 and 3 is not allowed.) Ans 1. 185 2. 195 3. 180 4. 190 Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009170391 Option 1 ID : 441009674478 Option 2 ID : 441009674480 Option 3 ID : 441009674477 Option 4 ID : 441009674479 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 11, "q": "Consider the following statements regarding the molecule of a compound. Which of the following statements is/are correct? Statement 1: A molecule of a compound must consist of atoms of at least two different elements. Statement 2: Ozone (O₃) is a molecule of a compound because it contains multiple oxygen atoms. Ans 1. Both Statements 1 and 2 are correct 2. Only Statement 2 is correct 3. Only Statement 1 is correct 4. Neither Statement 1 nor 2 is correct Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100971294 Option 1 ID : 441009283577 Option 2 ID : 441009283576 Option 3 ID : 441009283575 Option 4 ID : 441009283578 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 12, "q": "Which legislation did the Government of India introduce in 2025 to modernise India's shipping laws by replacing the colonial-era Indian Bills of Lading Act of 1856? Ans 1. The Indian Ocean Navigation Act, 2025 2. The Bills of Lading Bill, 2025 3. The Maritime Trade and Commerce Act, 2025 4. The Shipping and Logistics Modernization Act, 2025 Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100977932 Option 1 ID : 441009309733 Option 2 ID : 441009309732 Option 3 ID : 441009309730 Option 4 ID : 441009309731 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 13, "q": "Which of the following is NOT a growth movement in plants? Ans 1. Shoots of plants grow upwards 2. Plants move their leaves in response to touch. 3. Roots of plants grow downwards 4. Growth of pollen tubes towards ovules Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100961461 Option 1 ID : 441009244888 Option 2 ID : 441009244886 Option 3 ID : 441009244887 Option 4 ID : 441009244889 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 14, "q": "Which of the following is one of the 17 United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs)? Ans 1. Technological monopolies 2. Zero hunger 3. Military expansion 4. Industrial isolation Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100977098 Option 1 ID : 441009306437 Option 2 ID : 441009306439 Option 3 ID : 441009306440 Option 4 ID : 441009306438 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 15, "q": "A student heats an unknown organic compound and a gas is released. This gas turns lime water milky but does not support combustion. Which of the following is the gas? Ans 1. Oxygen 2. Hydrogen 3. Carbon dioxide 4. Methane Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100968999 Option 1 ID : 441009274630 Option 2 ID : 441009274629 Option 3 ID : 441009274631 Option 4 ID : 441009274632 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 16, "q": "The principal axis of a spherical mirror is _____. Ans 1. parallel to the mirror at its pole 2. inclined at an angle of 45° to the pole 3. inclined at an angle of 60° to the pole 4. normal to the mirror at its pole Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100995404 Option 1 ID : 441009379573 Option 2 ID : 441009379574 Option 3 ID : 441009379575 Option 4 ID : 441009379572 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 17, "q": "The volume of a solid cylinder is 40194 cm3 and its height is 29 cm. What is the total surface area of the solid cylinder? (Nearest to an integer) Ans 1. 6577 cm2 2. 6634 cm2 3. 6567 cm2 4. 6600 cm2 Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009170071 Option 1 ID : 441009673200 Option 2 ID : 441009673198 Option 3 ID : 441009673199 Option 4 ID : 441009673197 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 18, "q": "In which of the following Vedas is the phrase 'Vasudhaiva Kutumbakam' mentioned? Ans 1. Mahabharata 2. Atharva Veda 3. Ramayana 4. Samveda Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100969352 Option 1 ID : 441009276029 Option 2 ID : 441009276030 Option 3 ID : 441009276028 Option 4 ID : 441009276031 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 19, "q": "Which of the following Fundamental Rights provides Indian citizens with the power to approach the Supreme Court of India for the enforcement of their rights? Ans 1. Right to Freedom of Speech and Expression 2. Right to Equality 3. Right to Freedom of Religion 4. Right to Constitutional Remedies Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100989271 Option 1 ID : 441009355221 Option 2 ID : 441009355219 Option 3 ID : 441009355222 Option 4 ID : 441009355220 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 20, "q": "Due to water crisis, 15% of the initial population left a town, and 60% of the remaining left the town for pursuing jobs. If 3400 people currently inhabit the town, what is the ratio of initial population to present population? Ans 1. 52:18 2. 50:17 3. 56:22 4. 55:24 Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009170040 Option 1 ID : 441009673075 Option 2 ID : 441009673073 Option 3 ID : 441009673076 Option 4 ID : 441009673074 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 21, "q": "Which of the following gases is produced when coal burns in insufficient oxygen? Ans 1. Nitrous oxide 2. Carbon dioxide 3. Carbon monoxide 4. Sulphur dioxide Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100969769 Option 1 ID : 441009277727 Option 2 ID : 441009277728 Option 3 ID : 441009277729 Option 4 ID : 441009277730 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 22, "q": "Which of the following Indian states are primarily covered by the Great Indian Desert? Ans 1. Uttar Pradesh and Bihar 2. Gujarat and Rajasthan 3. Maharashtra and Madhya Pradesh 4. Uttar Pradesh and Uttarakhand Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100977642 Option 1 ID : 441009308524 Option 2 ID : 441009308527 Option 3 ID : 441009308525 Option 4 ID : 441009308526 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 23, "q": "Ans 1. 2. 3. 4. Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009170055 Option 1 ID : 441009673134 Option 2 ID : 441009673135 Option 3 ID : 441009673136 Option 4 ID : 441009673133 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 24, "q": "Which of the following statements is NOT true about resistors connected in parallel? Ans 1. The reciprocal of the total resistance is equal to the sum of the reciprocals of individual resistances. 2. The total resistance is less than the smallest individual resistance. 3. The voltage across each resistor is the same. 4. The current through each resistor is the same. Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009105881 Option 1 ID : 441009421591 Option 2 ID : 441009421592 Option 3 ID : 441009421589 Option 4 ID : 441009421590 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 25, "q": "Which Article of the Indian Constitution provides High Courts with the power to issue writs for the enforcement of Fundamental Rights and for any other purpose? Ans 1. Article 226 2. Article 141 3. Article 32 4. Article 368 Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100989710 Option 1 ID : 441009357007 Option 2 ID : 441009357006 Option 3 ID : 441009357008 Option 4 ID : 441009357005 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 26, "q": "  Ans 1. 2. 3. 4. Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100986138 Option 1 ID : 441009342271 Option 2 ID : 441009342272 Option 3 ID : 441009342273 Option 4 ID : 441009342270 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 27, "q": "Which of the following is CORRECT regarding the female gamete? Ans 1. The female gamete (egg cells) is large, motile, and not contains stored food. 2. The female gamete (egg cells) is small, motile, and not contains stored food. 3. The female gamete (egg cells) is small, motile, and contains stored food. 4. The female gamete (egg cells) is large, non-motile, and contains stored food. Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100967294 Option 1 ID : 441009267925 Option 2 ID : 441009267924 Option 3 ID : 441009267922 Option 4 ID : 441009267923 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 28, "q": "Which acclaimed Indian filmmaker, known for pioneering the 'parallel cinema' movement, passed away on 23 December 2024? Ans 1. Satyajit Ray 2. Mrinal Sen 3. Shyam Benegal 4. Adoor Gopalakrishnan Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100975822 Option 1 ID : 441009301562 Option 2 ID : 441009301564 Option 3 ID : 441009301563 Option 4 ID : 441009301565 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 29, "q": "A man travels from point A to B at a speed of 55 km/h and returns to A through same route by increasing his speed by 50% of his earlier speed. His average speed (in km/h) for the whole journey is: Ans 1. 67 2. 66 3. 63 4. 69 Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009170066 Option 1 ID : 441009673178 Option 2 ID : 441009673177 Option 3 ID : 441009673180 Option 4 ID : 441009673179 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 30, "q": "Mithila painting, also known as Madhubani folk art, is traditionally associated with which Indian state? Ans 1. West Bengal 2. Uttar Pradesh 3. Rajasthan 4. Bihar Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100973466 Option 1 ID : 441009292175 Option 2 ID : 441009292177 Option 3 ID : 441009292174 Option 4 ID : 441009292176 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : -- Section : Professional Ability", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 1, "q": "The primary test to identify Pseudomonas aeruginosa in the laboratory is______________. Ans 1. Catalase test 2. Nitrate reduction test 3. Oxidase test (positive) 4. Coagulase test Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160119 Option 1 ID : 441009634774 Option 2 ID : 441009634777 Option 3 ID : 441009634776 Option 4 ID : 441009634775 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 31, "q": "The symptom of elephantiasis, i.e. chronic obstructive lesions is seen after _________ years from the onset of the first acute attack. Ans 1. 1-5 2. 15-20 3. 5-10 4. 10-15 Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009164870 Option 1 ID : 441009653113 Option 2 ID : 441009653116 Option 3 ID : 441009653114 Option 4 ID : 441009653115 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 32, "q": "A patient complaints of severe chest pain not relieved by rest, position change, or nitrate administration, these symptoms indicate patient is suffering from _________. Ans 1. Stable angina 2. Unstable Angina 3. Nocturnal angina 4. Myocardial infraction Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009162426 Option 1 ID : 441009643358 Option 2 ID : 441009643356 Option 3 ID : 441009643359 Option 4 ID : 441009643357 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 33, "q": "Which of the following is NOT a recognised risk factor for the development of renal carcinoma Ans 1. Hypertension 2. Smoking 3. Hemodialysis 4. Obesity Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009193930 Option 1 ID : 441009763716 Option 2 ID : 441009763715 Option 3 ID : 441009763713 Option 4 ID : 441009763714 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 34, "q": "Which of the following fetal/neonatal complication is associated with hypertensive disorder during pregnancy? Ans 1. Intrauterine growth restriction 2. Hypercalcemia 3. Macrosomia 4. Delayed lung maturation Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160642 Option 1 ID : 441009636392 Option 2 ID : 441009636391 Option 3 ID : 441009636393 Option 4 ID : 441009636394 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 35, "q": "Which determinants of health believes that if the environment is favorable to the individual, he can make full use of his physical and mental capabilities? Ans 1. Health services 2. Biological 3. socio-cultural conditions 4. Environment Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009164875 Option 1 ID : 441009653133 Option 2 ID : 441009653135 Option 3 ID : 441009653134 Option 4 ID : 441009653136 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 36, "q": "A major complication associated with prolonged retention of a dead foetus (>4 weeks) is ________________. Ans 1. gestational diabetes 2. preeclampsia 3. preterm labour 4. disseminated intravascular coagulation (DIC) Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160498 Option 1 ID : 441009635936 Option 2 ID : 441009635934 Option 3 ID : 441009635937 Option 4 ID : 441009635935 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 37, "q": "Which of the following is not the solid form for administration of drugs by oral route ? Ans 1. Enteriac coated tablet 2. Caplet 3. Elixir 4. Capsule Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009159843 Option 1 ID : 441009634055 Option 2 ID : 441009634056 Option 3 ID : 441009634058 Option 4 ID : 441009634057 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 38, "q": "In which psychotherapy, the nurse sets a goal to create a safe secure and therapeutic environment to maximize recovery and enhancing patient’s autonomy? Ans 1. Social therapy 2. Behaviour therapy 3. Milieu therapy 4. Supportive therapy Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009162248 Option 1 ID : 441009642646 Option 2 ID : 441009642647 Option 3 ID : 441009642645 Option 4 ID : 441009642648 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 39, "q": "Which of the following medications can worsen anaphylactic shock by blocking the effects of epinephrine? Ans 1. ACE inhibitors 2. Beta-blockers 3. Antihistamines 4. Corticosteroids Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160259 Option 1 ID : 441009635303 Option 2 ID : 441009635304 Option 3 ID : 441009635305 Option 4 ID : 441009635306 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 40, "q": "In which method of delivery for the aftercoming head, the baby is allowed to hang by its own weight for delivery of head? Ans 1. Modified Mauriceau-Smellie-Veit technique 2. Breech extraction 3. Burns-Marshall method 4. Forceps delivery Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009162657 Option 1 ID : 441009644280 Option 2 ID : 441009644283 Option 3 ID : 441009644281 Option 4 ID : 441009644282 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 41, "q": "In atherosclerosis accumulation of lipid or fatty substances and fibrous tissue present in Ans 1. Vein 2. Mucosa 3. Muscle 4. Artery Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009194734 Option 1 ID : 441009766883 Option 2 ID : 441009766885 Option 3 ID : 441009766886 Option 4 ID : 441009766884 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 42, "q": "Which theory of culture applies to the concept of biological evolution to the growth of human knowledge? Ans 1. Evolutionary epistemology 2. Cultural particularism 3. Dual inheritance theory 4. Multilinear theory Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009162279 Option 1 ID : 441009642771 Option 2 ID : 441009642770 Option 3 ID : 441009642769 Option 4 ID : 441009642772 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 43, "q": "In which condition, collar sling is applied as first aid measure before shifting the patient to hospital? Ans 1. Fracture upper leg 2. Fracture upper arm 3. Fracture spine 4. Fracture lower arm Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009162864 Option 1 ID : 441009645098 Option 2 ID : 441009645096 Option 3 ID : 441009645099 Option 4 ID : 441009645097 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 44, "q": "Which of the muscle dysfunction results in Urinary retention ? Ans 1. dartos 2. cremaster muscles 3. Detrusor Muscles 4. Levator ani Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009174827 Option 1 ID : 441009691550 Option 2 ID : 441009691551 Option 3 ID : 441009691548 Option 4 ID : 441009691549 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 45, "q": "Which of the following is NOT typically considered a social determinant of nutritional status? Ans 1. Genetic factors 2. Cultural food practices 3. Food environment 4. Income level Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160754 Option 1 ID : 441009636788 Option 2 ID : 441009636789 Option 3 ID : 441009636787 Option 4 ID : 441009636786 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 46, "q": "The Reporting guidelines followed for randomized Controlled trial is Ans 1. CARE 2. CONSORT 3. STROBE 4. PRISM Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009190437 Option 1 ID : 441009750736 Option 2 ID : 441009750733 Option 3 ID : 441009750734 Option 4 ID : 441009750735 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 47, "q": "Which chemotherapeutic agent is used to treat colorectal cancer and works by inhibiting thymidylate synthase? Ans 1. Paclitaxel 2. 5-Fluorouracil (5-FU) 3. Etoposide 4. Cyclophosphamide Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160188 Option 1 ID : 441009635041 Option 2 ID : 441009635039 Option 3 ID : 441009635040 Option 4 ID : 441009635038 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 48, "q": "Which artery supplies blood to the muscles of the proximal leg and knee joint? Ans 1. Lateral planter artery 2. Peroneal artery 3. Inferior Mesentric artery 4. Popliteal artery Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009158508 Option 1 ID : 441009628971 Option 2 ID : 441009628974 Option 3 ID : 441009628973 Option 4 ID : 441009628972 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 49, "q": "Which of the following activities is an example of secondary prevention? Ans 1. The patient attends cardiac rehabilitation sessions 2. A 50-year-old woman with no history of disease attends the 3. A home health care nurse visits a patient’s home to change 4. The school health nurse provides a program to the firstyear Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160095 Option 1 ID : 441009634681 Option 2 ID : 441009634679 Option 3 ID : 441009634678 Option 4 ID : 441009634680 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 50, "q": "Which of the following is the most comprehensive definition of health? Ans 1. Health is the state of having no chronic illnesses. 2. Health is a holistic state that includes physical, mental, and social well-being. 3. Health is the ability to perform physical activities without discomfort. 4. Health is the absence of disease or disability. Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009159868 Option 1 ID : 441009634120 Option 2 ID : 441009634121 Option 3 ID : 441009634119 Option 4 ID : 441009634122 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 51, "q": "Which of the following is the best method to ensure health messages reach people with hearing impairments? Ans 1. Phone calls 2. Radio campaigns 3. Visual materials with clear illustrations 4. Loud verbal announcements Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160955 Option 1 ID : 441009637509 Option 2 ID : 441009637508 Option 3 ID : 441009637507 Option 4 ID : 441009637506 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 52, "q": "In assessing fluid status in a patient with acute kidney injury, which physical finding best indicates fluid deficit? Ans 1. Bibasilar crackles 2. Bounding peripheral pulses 3. Poor skin turgor and dry mucous membranes 4. Periorbital oedema Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160355 Option 1 ID : 441009635650 Option 2 ID : 441009635649 Option 3 ID : 441009635651 Option 4 ID : 441009635652 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 53, "q": "The decrease in carbonic acid seen in hyperventilation is called as Ans 1. Respiratory acidosis 2. Respirarory Alkalosis 3. metabolic alkalosis 4. metabolic acidosis Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009174186 Option 1 ID : 441009689148 Option 2 ID : 441009689149 Option 3 ID : 441009689151 Option 4 ID : 441009689150 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 54, "q": "In which breech presentation, the presenting part consists of the two buttocks and external genitalia only? Ans 1. Footling presentation 2. Knee presentation 3. Flexed breech presentation 4. Frank breech presentation Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009162649 Option 1 ID : 441009644250 Option 2 ID : 441009644251 Option 3 ID : 441009644249 Option 4 ID : 441009644248 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 55, "q": "What is a sign of fetal death in the womb? Ans 1. No heartbeat 2. Fetal tachycardia 3. Increased fetal movements 4. Increased amniotic fluid Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160508 Option 1 ID : 441009635953 Option 2 ID : 441009635951 Option 3 ID : 441009635954 Option 4 ID : 441009635952 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 56, "q": "Increase risk of coronary heart disease and atherosclerosis is due to increase in ___________. Ans 1. HDL cholesterol 2. LDL cholesterol 3. VLDL cholesterol 4. Triglycerides Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009159759 Option 1 ID : 441009633837 Option 2 ID : 441009633835 Option 3 ID : 441009633836 Option 4 ID : 441009633838 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 57, "q": "Which symptom should the nurse assess when a patient receives loop diuretics? Ans 1. Paresthesias and irritability 2. Increased blood pressure and muscle spasm 3. Weak, irregular pulse, and poor muscle tone 4. Restlessness and agitation Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160251 Option 1 ID : 441009635272 Option 2 ID : 441009635274 Option 3 ID : 441009635273 Option 4 ID : 441009635271 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 58, "q": "What is the recommended daily calcium requirement for a sedentary Indian woman? Ans 1. 600 mg/dl 2. 500 mg/dl 3. 400 mg/dl 4. 700 mg/dl Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009159770 Option 1 ID : 441009633874 Option 2 ID : 441009633873 Option 3 ID : 441009633872 Option 4 ID : 441009633875 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 59, "q": "Janani Suraksha yojana(JSY ) is safe motherhood intervention under Ans 1. National Rural Health mission 2. Indra Dhanush Mission 2.0 3. National Urban Health mission 4. Ayushman Bharath Mission Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009186150 Option 1 ID : 441009735906 Option 2 ID : 441009735908 Option 3 ID : 441009735907 Option 4 ID : 441009735909 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 60, "q": "Which element of counselling refers to the genuine, authentic presence of the counselor? Ans 1. Congruence 2. Intelligence 3. Directiveness 4. Authority Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160971 Option 1 ID : 441009637580 Option 2 ID : 441009637581 Option 3 ID : 441009637583 Option 4 ID : 441009637582 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 61, "q": "For Indvidual's with mental retardation, during play therapy the nurse should consider Ans 1. using complex and abstract play material 2. focussing on cognitive development 3. ignoring individual difference 4. tailoring play task according to intellectual level Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009194891 Option 1 ID : 441009767499 Option 2 ID : 441009767500 Option 3 ID : 441009767502 Option 4 ID : 441009767501 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 62, "q": "In burns, the associated tissue damage with greatest destruction occurs in: Ans 1. Zone of hyperemia 2. Zone of stasis 3. Zone of coagulation 4. Zone of Hyperperfusion Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009194938 Option 1 ID : 441009767685 Option 2 ID : 441009767683 Option 3 ID : 441009767686 Option 4 ID : 441009767684 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 63, "q": "In case of suspected placenta previa the vaginal examination is advisable Ans 1. after ruling out previa by ultrasound 2. to determine placental abnormalities 3. to detect the congenital abnormalities 4. to determine fetal position Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009183771 Option 1 ID : 441009726475 Option 2 ID : 441009726476 Option 3 ID : 441009726477 Option 4 ID : 441009726478 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 64, "q": "Which of the following best describes the role of the paranasal sinuses in respiration? Ans 1. They enhance the voice resonance and lighten the skull 2. They produce surfactant for efficient gas exchange 3. They regulate the pH of inhaled air 4. They filter and warm the air before it reaches the lungs Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009159719 Option 1 ID : 441009633687 Option 2 ID : 441009633688 Option 3 ID : 441009633689 Option 4 ID : 441009633686 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 65, "q": "The purpose of performing the Arthrocentesis is: Ans 1. Bone mass 2. Muscle contraction 3. Blood flow abnormalities 4. Synovial fluid analysis Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009194007 Option 1 ID : 441009763975 Option 2 ID : 441009763977 Option 3 ID : 441009763976 Option 4 ID : 441009763978 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 66, "q": "Who is considered the pioneer of nursing research and published 'Notes on Nursing' in 1859? Ans 1. Florence Nightingale 2. Hildegard Peplau 3. Martha Rogers 4. Virginia Henderson Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160936 Option 1 ID : 441009637450 Option 2 ID : 441009637449 Option 3 ID : 441009637452 Option 4 ID : 441009637451 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 67, "q": "The morphology of reversible cell injury seen includes: Ans 1. Metabolic change 2. Hydropic change 3. Osseus change 4. Oxidative change Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009194975 Option 1 ID : 441009767832 Option 2 ID : 441009767831 Option 3 ID : 441009767834 Option 4 ID : 441009767833 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 68, "q": "The effect of single dose triamterene lasts for how many hours? Ans 1. 12-16 hours 2. 18-20 hours 3. >20 hours 4. 6-8 hours Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160212 Option 1 ID : 441009635135 Option 2 ID : 441009635136 Option 3 ID : 441009635137 Option 4 ID : 441009635134 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 69, "q": "Which of the following is a morphological pathological process occurs in irreversible cell injury? Ans 1. Mucoid change 2. Hydropic change 3. Hyaline change 4. Autolysis change Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009162368 Option 1 ID : 441009643127 Option 2 ID : 441009643125 Option 3 ID : 441009643126 Option 4 ID : 441009643124 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 70, "q": "Which extraocular muscle is primarily responsible for abduction of the eye and outward rotation of the eyeball? Ans 1. Superior rectus 2. Medial rectus 3. Lateral rectus 4. Inferior rectus Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009159732 Option 1 ID : 441009633738 Option 2 ID : 441009633741 Option 3 ID : 441009633740 Option 4 ID : 441009633739 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}]});
window.PYQ_OCR['rrb-para'].push({t:'rrb para 2025 04 29 shift 3',q:[{"n": 1, "q": "A concave mirror with a focal length 'f' is cut into two equal halves along the principal axis. What happens to the focal length of each half? Ans 1. It doubles to 2f. 2. It remains f. 3. It becomes undefined. 4. It becomes f/2. Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100995417 Option 1 ID : 441009379626 Option 2 ID : 441009379624 Option 3 ID : 441009379627 Option 4 ID : 441009379625 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 2, "q": "Which of the following factors determines the colour of scattered light in the atmosphere, according to the Tyndall effect? Ans 1. Colour of the scattering particle 2. It does not depend on the scattering particle. 3. Size of the scattering particle 4. Density of the scattering particle Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100997903 Option 1 ID : 441009389667 Option 2 ID : 441009389668 Option 3 ID : 441009389666 Option 4 ID : 441009389665 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 3, "q": "Ans 1. 2. 3. 4. Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009170049 Option 1 ID : 441009673110 Option 2 ID : 441009673111 Option 3 ID : 441009673109 Option 4 ID : 441009673112 Not Attempted and Status : Marked For Review Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 4, "q": "Which of the following statements is true for displacement reactions? Ans 1. A less reactive element replaces a more reactive one. 2. A more reactive element replaces a less reactive one. 3. They require only heat to proceed. 4. They only occur in non-metals. Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100970231 Option 1 ID : 441009279542 Option 2 ID : 441009279541 Option 3 ID : 441009279544 Option 4 ID : 441009279543 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 5, "q": "Which of the following statements about molecules of elements is correct? Ans 1. Molecular oxygen and ozone are both molecules of the same element. 2. All elements exist as monoatomic molecules in nature. 3. Diatomic molecules only contain atoms of different elements. 4. A molecule of phosphorus always contains five atoms. Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100971283 Option 1 ID : 441009283525 Option 2 ID : 441009283523 Option 3 ID : 441009283524 Option 4 ID : 441009283526 Not Attempted and Status : Marked For Review Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 6, "q": "A man travels from point A to B at a speed of 11 km/hr and returns to A through same route by increasing his speed by 75% of his earlier speed. His average speed (in km/hr) for the whole journey is: Ans 1. 16 2. 14 3. 18 4. 10 Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009170067 Option 1 ID : 441009673184 Option 2 ID : 441009673181 Option 3 ID : 441009673183 Option 4 ID : 441009673182 Not Attempted and Status : Marked For Review Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 7, "q": "In a certain code language, ‘A + B’ means ‘A is the father of B’, ‘A – B’ means ‘A is the husband of B’, ‘A × B’ means ‘A is the wife of B’ and ‘A ÷ B’ means ‘A is the daughter of B’. How is V related to Z if ‘V ÷ W × X + Y – Z’? Ans 1. Husband's sister 2. Mother’s brother 3. Mother’s mother 4. Brother’s wife Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009170429 Option 1 ID : 441009674629 Option 2 ID : 441009674631 Option 3 ID : 441009674630 Option 4 ID : 441009674632 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 8, "q": "Where was the 2012 United Nations Climate Change Conference held? Ans 1. Durban 2. Copenhagen 3. Stockholm 4. Doha Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100976970 Option 1 ID : 441009305996 Option 2 ID : 441009305993 Option 3 ID : 441009305994 Option 4 ID : 441009305995 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 9, "q": "Two sets of numbers are given below. In each set of numbers, certain mathematical operation(s) on the first number results in the second number. Similarly, certain mathematical operation(s) on the second number results in the third number and so on. Which of the given options follows the same set of operations as in the given sets? (Note: Operations should be performed on the whole numbers, without breaking down the numbers into their constituent digits. E.g., 13 – Operations on 13 such as adding/subtracting/multiplying to 13 can be performed. Breaking down 13 into 1 and 3 and then performing mathematical operations on 1 and 3 is not allowed.) 155 – 125 – 100 – 80; 125 – 95 – 70 – 50 Ans 1. 95 – 70 – 45 – 35 2. 100 – 70 – 45 – 25 3. 140 – 110 – 85 – 60 4. 80 – 50 – 35 – 15 Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009170389 Option 1 ID : 441009674470 Option 2 ID : 441009674471 Option 3 ID : 441009674472 Option 4 ID : 441009674469 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 10, "q": "Which of the following describes the process by which the concentration of toxic substances, such as pesticides, increases in organisms at higher levels of the food chain? Ans 1. Biological magnification 2. Biological oxygen demand 3. Food web 4. Ecological pyramid Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100972872 Option 1 ID : 441009289815 Option 2 ID : 441009289812 Option 3 ID : 441009289814 Option 4 ID : 441009289813 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 11, "q": "In December 2024, Prime Minister Narendra Modi was honoured with Kuwait's highest civilian award. What is the name of the award?​ Ans 1. Order of Mubarak Al-Kabeer​ 2. Order of Zayed 3. Order of Abdulaziz Al Saud 4. Order of the Nile Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100975778 Option 1 ID : 441009301378 Option 2 ID : 441009301380 Option 3 ID : 441009301381 Option 4 ID : 441009301379 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 12, "q": "The semi-cryogenic engine tested by ISRO in 2025 primarily uses which fuel? Ans 1. Methane and Liquid Oxygen (LOX) 2. Solid Composite Propellant 3. Liquid Hydrogen (LH2) and Liquid Oxygen (LOX) 4. Kerosene (RP-1) and Liquid Oxygen (LOX) Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100977983 Option 1 ID : 441009309932 Option 2 ID : 441009309933 Option 3 ID : 441009309930 Option 4 ID : 441009309931 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 13, "q": "Which immediate cause triggered the Sanyasi Uprisings in Bengal lasting from 1770 to the 1820s? Ans 1. The confiscation of peasant lands following the famine 2. Heavy taxation on local handicrafts 3. Forced recruitment of local soldiers into the British army 4. Restrictions imposed by the British on pilgrims visiting holy sites Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100984036 Option 1 ID : 441009333879 Option 2 ID : 441009333876 Option 3 ID : 441009333877 Option 4 ID : 441009333878 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 14, "q": "Kalpana and Sudha got 574 and 553 marks, respectively, in an examination. If Kalpana scored 82% marks, then what is the percentage of marks scored by Sudha? Ans 1. 79% 2. 76% 3. 77% 4. 81% Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009170041 Option 1 ID : 441009673077 Option 2 ID : 441009673078 Option 3 ID : 441009673080 Option 4 ID : 441009673079 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 15, "q": "What is the maximum value that must be assigned to A so that the 8-digit number 489A5384 is divisible by 4? Ans 1. 5 2. 4 3. 8 4. 9 Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009170058 Option 1 ID : 441009673147 Option 2 ID : 441009673148 Option 3 ID : 441009673146 Option 4 ID : 441009673145 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 16, "q": "Under which of the following Constitutional Amendments were the Fundamental Duties incorporated into the Indian Constitution? Ans 1. 61st Amendment Act, 1988 2. 42nd Amendment Act, 1976 3. 44th Amendment Act, 1978 4. 52nd Amendment Act, 1986 Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100989096 Option 1 ID : 441009354475 Option 2 ID : 441009354478 Option 3 ID : 441009354477 Option 4 ID : 441009354476 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 17, "q": "Which of the following statements is FALSE? Ans 1. The resistance of a conductor is inversely proportional to its cross-sectional area. 2. The resistance of a conductor is independent of its material. 3. The resistance of a wire decreases when a thicker wire of the same material is used. 4. The resistance of a wire increases when its length is doubled. Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009105874 Option 1 ID : 441009421568 Option 2 ID : 441009421567 Option 3 ID : 441009421566 Option 4 ID : 441009421565 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 18, "q": "Six toy cars Car1, Car2, Car3 Car4, Car5 and Car6 are kept around a circular table facing inside, not necessarily in the same order. Car4 is second to the left of Car6. Car5 is kept to the immediate right of Car2. Car2 is second to the right of Car3. Car3 is to the immediate right of Car4. If we start counting the number of cars towards the left of Car5, then how many cars are kept between Car6 and Car5? Ans 1. Two 2. Three 3. One 4. Zero Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009170425 Option 1 ID : 441009674615 Option 2 ID : 441009674614 Option 3 ID : 441009674613 Option 4 ID : 441009674616 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 19, "q": "Under which Indian government scheme launched in 2000 is additional central assistance given to states for basic services such as primary health, primary education, rural shelter, rural drinking water and rural electrification? Ans 1. Rural Employment Generation Programme (REGP) 2. Swarnajayanti Gram Swarozgar Yojana (SGSY) 3. Prime Minister Rozgar Yozana (PMRY) 4. Pradhan Mantri Gramodaya Yozana (PMGY) Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100993459 Option 1 ID : 441009371738 Option 2 ID : 441009371740 Option 3 ID : 441009371739 Option 4 ID : 441009371737 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 20, "q": "Which notable water body is located to the south of the Mahanadi Delta on the Eastern Coastal Plains of India? Ans 1. Dal Lake 2. Vembanad Lagoon 3. Chilka Lake 4. Sambhar Salt Lake Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100977592 Option 1 ID : 441009308317 Option 2 ID : 441009308318 Option 3 ID : 441009308319 Option 4 ID : 441009308316 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 21, "q": "Which part of the brain control Involuntary actions, including blood pressure, salivation, and vomiting? Ans 1. Thalamus in the fore brain 2. Cerebrum in the fore brain 3. Medulla in the hind brain 4. Pons in the hind brain Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100971462 Option 1 ID : 441009284234 Option 2 ID : 441009284233 Option 3 ID : 441009284231 Option 4 ID : 441009284232 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 22, "q": "Which of the following letter-number clusters will replace the question mark (?) in the given series to make it logically complete? MIN29, SOT50, YUZ71, EAF92, ? Ans 1. KLL113 2. PGL113 3. KGL113 4. KGO113 Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009170411 Option 1 ID : 441009674557 Option 2 ID : 441009674558 Option 3 ID : 441009674559 Option 4 ID : 441009674560 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 23, "q": "If the lateral surface area of a cylinder is 498.2 cm2 and its height is 41 cm, then find its volume. (Use π = 3.14 and round off to two decimal places) Ans 1. 516.58 cm3 2. 510.22 cm3 3. 505.79 cm3 4. 481.99 cm3 Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009170070 Option 1 ID : 441009673196 Option 2 ID : 441009673195 Option 3 ID : 441009673194 Option 4 ID : 441009673193 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 24, "q": "What should come in place of the question mark (?) in the given series based on the English alphabetical order? FAT HDV JGX LJZ ? Ans 1. PNC 2. OMD 3. OLA 4. NMB Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009170400 Option 1 ID : 441009674514 Option 2 ID : 441009674515 Option 3 ID : 441009674513 Option 4 ID : 441009674516 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 25, "q": "Transfer of pollen occurring in the same flower is known as___. Ans 1. Hybridization 2. Cross-pollination 3. Self-pollination 4. Fertilization Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100967336 Option 1 ID : 441009268099 Option 2 ID : 441009268098 Option 3 ID : 441009268101 Option 4 ID : 441009268100 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 26, "q": "From which Harappan site was the ‘Dancing Girl’, a bronze figurine, discovered? Ans 1. Lothal 2. Dholavira 3. Mohenjo-daro 4. Harappa Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100973270 Option 1 ID : 441009291393 Option 2 ID : 441009291394 Option 3 ID : 441009291392 Option 4 ID : 441009291391 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 27, "q": "Which branch of the Indian Armed Forces participated in the 6th edition of Dharma Guardian? Ans 1. Indian Army 2. Indian Air Force 3. Indian Navy 4. Indian Coast Guard Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100975885 Option 1 ID : 441009301816 Option 2 ID : 441009301814 Option 3 ID : 441009301815 Option 4 ID : 441009301817 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 28, "q": "Which Parliamentary Committee reviews reports submitted by Public Undertakings specified in the Fourth Schedule to the Rules of Procedure and Conduct of Business in the Lok Sabha of India? Ans 1. Committee on Public Undertakings 2. Estimates Committee 3. Public Accounts Committee 4. Select Committee on Financial Oversight Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100989733 Option 1 ID : 441009357100 Option 2 ID : 441009357098 Option 3 ID : 441009357099 Option 4 ID : 441009357097 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 29, "q": "Which of the following methods is NOT used to extract metals that are placed in the middle of the reactivity series from their ores? Ans 1. Calcination followed by reduction with carbon 2. Displacement using a more reactive metal 3. Heating their sulphide ores directly in the presence of carbon 4. Roasting followed by reduction with carbon Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100971233 Option 1 ID : 441009283326 Option 2 ID : 441009283324 Option 3 ID : 441009283325 Option 4 ID : 441009283323 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 30, "q": "Which of the following is CORRECT regarding the plant tissue? Ans 1. Vascular tissue includes parenchyma, collenchyma, and sclerenchyma 2. Simple permanent tissue includes xylem and phloem 3. Meristematic tissues are responsible for plant growth. 4. Complex permanent tissue includes parenchyma, collenchyma, and sclerenchyma Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 44100965867 Option 1 ID : 441009262421 Option 2 ID : 441009262419 Option 3 ID : 441009262418 Option 4 ID : 441009262420 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : -- Section : Professional Ability", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 1, "q": "Which immunity leads to development of autoimmune disorders in an individual? Ans 1. Natural immunity 2. Active immunity 3. Passive immunity 4. Autoimmunity Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009159607 Option 1 ID : 441009633246 Option 2 ID : 441009633248 Option 3 ID : 441009633247 Option 4 ID : 441009633249 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 31, "q": "In third stage of labour, patient experiences intermittent discomfort in the lower abdomen during expulsion of placenta, it is due to__________. Ans 1. Episiotomy 2. Dilation of vagina 3. Distention of bladder 4. Uterine contraction Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009162734 Option 1 ID : 441009644590 Option 2 ID : 441009644591 Option 3 ID : 441009644588 Option 4 ID : 441009644589 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 32, "q": "The risk factor of hypercalcemia is Ans 1. Prolonged immobilization 2. Alcohol 3. Malabsorption 4. Sepsis Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009183074 Option 1 ID : 441009723713 Option 2 ID : 441009723710 Option 3 ID : 441009723711 Option 4 ID : 441009723712 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 33, "q": "In which among the following wound healing process the synthesis of collagen occur Ans 1. Maturation phase 2. Inflammatory phase 3. Haemostasis phase 4. Granulation phase Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009183004 Option 1 ID : 441009723437 Option 2 ID : 441009723434 Option 3 ID : 441009723435 Option 4 ID : 441009723436 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 34, "q": "Which of the following is not an indication for genetic counseling in a pregnant women Ans 1. Routine pregnancy checkup without any concern 2. A family history of known genetic condition 3. Consanguinity 4. Advanced maternal age Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009185481 Option 1 ID : 441009733246 Option 2 ID : 441009733247 Option 3 ID : 441009733245 Option 4 ID : 441009733244 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 35, "q": "Early puerperium begins as soon as the placenta is expelled and lasts__________. Ans 1. up to 6 months 2. up to 6 weeks 3. up to 7 days 4. within 24 hours Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009162786 Option 1 ID : 441009644791 Option 2 ID : 441009644790 Option 3 ID : 441009644789 Option 4 ID : 441009644788 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 36, "q": "What is the first step in providing first aid for a snake bite? Ans 1. Cut the wound and try to suck out the venom 2. Make the person walk to seek medical help 3. Keep the affected limb immobilized and below heart level 4. Apply ice to the bite area Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160099 Option 1 ID : 441009634696 Option 2 ID : 441009634697 Option 3 ID : 441009634695 Option 4 ID : 441009634694 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 37, "q": "Which factor increases heart rates of firing during exercise? Ans 1. Chemoreceptors 2. Baroreceptors 3. Proprioreceptors 4. Autonomic nervous system Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009159659 Option 1 ID : 441009633457 Option 2 ID : 441009633454 Option 3 ID : 441009633455 Option 4 ID : 441009633456 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 38, "q": "The amount of heat energy that is liberated by burning 1 gm of foodstuff completely in the presence of O2 is called ________. Ans 1. Calorie 2. Calorific Value 3. Basal Metabolic Rate 4. Specific Dynamic Action Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009159778 Option 1 ID : 441009633898 Option 2 ID : 441009633897 Option 3 ID : 441009633899 Option 4 ID : 441009633900 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 39, "q": "Chronic gout is characterised by multiple joint involvement with the presence of: Ans 1. Podagra 2. Pain 3. Tophi 4. Bursae Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009179772 Option 1 ID : 441009710462 Option 2 ID : 441009710464 Option 3 ID : 441009710463 Option 4 ID : 441009710465 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 40, "q": "Which route is used to administer chemotherapeutic agent to minimize the associated physical discomforts and risks of infection and infiltration by intravenous method? Ans 1. Central venous route 2. Intra-ossicle route 3. Trans-patch on skin 4. Intra-atrial route Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009162594 Option 1 ID : 441009644028 Option 2 ID : 441009644029 Option 3 ID : 441009644031 Option 4 ID : 441009644030 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 41, "q": "Which of the following is a warning sign of mental illness? Ans 1. Accepts self and others 2. Desires or demands immediate gratification 3. Uses sound judgements to make decisions 4. Inability to cope with problems and daily activities Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009162243 Option 1 ID : 441009642627 Option 2 ID : 441009642625 Option 3 ID : 441009642628 Option 4 ID : 441009642626 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 42, "q": "Which of the following activity should be avoided by a patient scheduled for a total ankle replacement surgery ? Ans 1. Bearing weight on the affected leg for 6 weeks 2. Lifting heavy objects 3. Abduction exercise of the affected ankle. 4. Sleeping on the back Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009193986 Option 1 ID : 441009763898 Option 2 ID : 441009763895 Option 3 ID : 441009763897 Option 4 ID : 441009763896 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 43, "q": "What does 'Nx' signify in the TNM classification? Ans 1. Regional lymph nodes cannot be assessed 2. Micrometastasis in lymph nodes 3. No lymph node involvement 4. Extensive lymph node involvement Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160390 Option 1 ID : 441009635725 Option 2 ID : 441009635727 Option 3 ID : 441009635724 Option 4 ID : 441009635726 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 44, "q": "Which of the following electrolytes should be monitored while administering Triamterene drug ? Ans 1. Chloride level 2. Potassium level 3. Sodium level 4. Bicarbonate level Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009182986 Option 1 ID : 441009723355 Option 2 ID : 441009723357 Option 3 ID : 441009723354 Option 4 ID : 441009723356 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 45, "q": "Which of the following is the most immediate priority in assessing disaster impact on a community? Ans 1. Environmental contamination 2. Threat to human life and safety 3. Infrastructure damage 4. Economic damage assessment Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160740 Option 1 ID : 441009636725 Option 2 ID : 441009636723 Option 3 ID : 441009636724 Option 4 ID : 441009636722 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 46, "q": "Which diagnostic method is recommended as the gold standard for malaria diagnosis under the National Programme? Ans 1. Rapid diagnostic tests only 2. Serological tests 3. Clinical symptoms only 4. Microscopic examination of blood smears Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160809 Option 1 ID : 441009636962 Option 2 ID : 441009636963 Option 3 ID : 441009636960 Option 4 ID : 441009636961 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 47, "q": "If a patient or relatives decide to leave the hospital against advice of the doctor, he/she has to sign___________ form before discharge. Ans 1. Abscond form 2. MLC form 3. NMLC form 4. LAMA form Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009162886 Option 1 ID : 441009645185 Option 2 ID : 441009645186 Option 3 ID : 441009645184 Option 4 ID : 441009645187 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 48, "q": "In which of the following grade does a tumour possess cells that are moderately differentiated? Ans 1. grade IV 2. grade I 3. grade II 4. grade III Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009193952 Option 1 ID : 441009763781 Option 2 ID : 441009763778 Option 3 ID : 441009763779 Option 4 ID : 441009763780 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 49, "q": "The main elements of the phospahte buffer system are Ans 1. NaCl and HHb 2. NaH2PO4 and NaCl 3. NaH2PO4 and NaHPO4 4. HHb and NaHPO4 Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009159809 Option 1 ID : 441009633987 Option 2 ID : 441009633986 Option 3 ID : 441009633989 Option 4 ID : 441009633988 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 50, "q": "Which laboratory finding is most consistent with acute DIC? Ans 1. Prolonged PT/PTT with thrombocytopenia 2. Elevated fibrinogen levels 3. Elevated platelet count 4. Decreased fibrin degradation products Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160342 Option 1 ID : 441009635599 Option 2 ID : 441009635600 Option 3 ID : 441009635597 Option 4 ID : 441009635598 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 51, "q": "In deep palpation method, the depth of skin depressed is approximately: Ans 1. 3-4 cm 2. 2-3 cm 3. 1-2 cm 4. 4-5cm Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009175804 Option 1 ID : 441009695245 Option 2 ID : 441009695246 Option 3 ID : 441009695247 Option 4 ID : 441009695244 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 52, "q": "The District Mental Health Program team typically includes all of the following, EXCEPT: Ans 1. a Psychiatric Social Worker 2. a Psychiatrist 3. a Neurosurgeon 4. a Clinical Psychologist Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160883 Option 1 ID : 441009637239 Option 2 ID : 441009637237 Option 3 ID : 441009637240 Option 4 ID : 441009637238 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 53, "q": "Which connective tissue forms supporting framework of liver, spleen and lymph nodes? Ans 1. Brown adipose tissue 2. White adipose tissue 3. Reticular connective tissue 4. Areolar connective tissue Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009159707 Option 1 ID : 441009633639 Option 2 ID : 441009633638 Option 3 ID : 441009633640 Option 4 ID : 441009633641 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 54, "q": "The microbes that use chemical compounds as a source of energy are known as: Ans 1. Lethotrophs 2. Organotrophs 3. Chemotrophs 4. Phototrophs Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009179996 Option 1 ID : 441009711307 Option 2 ID : 441009711309 Option 3 ID : 441009711308 Option 4 ID : 441009711306 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 55, "q": "When there is necrosis of the tissue due to burn injury, the patient is at risk of developing _____. Ans 1. Neutropenia 2. Disseminated intravascular coagulation 3. Thrombocytopenia 4. Haemorrhage Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009162512 Option 1 ID : 441009643703 Option 2 ID : 441009643701 Option 3 ID : 441009643700 Option 4 ID : 441009643702 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 56, "q": "The normal tissue present at an ectopic site, which is not a true tumour is known as: Ans 1. Choristoma 2. Hamartoma 3. Teratoma 4. Chondroma Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009195080 Option 1 ID : 441009768249 Option 2 ID : 441009768248 Option 3 ID : 441009768247 Option 4 ID : 441009768250 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 57, "q": "In Indian context, UHID in hospital commonly refers to: Ans 1. Union Health Identification 2. Uniform Health Identification 3. Unique Health Identification 4. User Health Identification Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009175905 Option 1 ID : 441009695642 Option 2 ID : 441009695640 Option 3 ID : 441009695641 Option 4 ID : 441009695643 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 58, "q": "From a physiological perspective, which of the following marks the beginning of the puerperium period? Ans 1. The first breastfeeding session 2. The rupture of membranes 3. The delivery of the placenta 4. The onset of labor Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160575 Option 1 ID : 441009636168 Option 2 ID : 441009636166 Option 3 ID : 441009636167 Option 4 ID : 441009636165 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 59, "q": "The important use of Goniometer is to measure the: Ans 1. Range of motion 2. Muscle strength 3. Muscle power 4. Muscle tone Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009175747 Option 1 ID : 441009695015 Option 2 ID : 441009695014 Option 3 ID : 441009695012 Option 4 ID : 441009695013 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 60, "q": "What is the most appropriate way to assess the effectiveness of nebulization therapy in a 4-year-old child? Ans 1. Count the number of coughs during treatment 2. Measure peak flow readings 3. Ask the child if breathing feels better 4. Monitor oxygen saturation and respiratory rate Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160618 Option 1 ID : 441009636298 Option 2 ID : 441009636297 Option 3 ID : 441009636295 Option 4 ID : 441009636296 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 61, "q": "The process of macrophages engulfs the microorganisms and cellular debris refers to Ans 1. Propulsion 2. ​Thrombopoisesis 3. Leukopoiesis 4. Phagocytosis Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009183048 Option 1 ID : 441009723607 Option 2 ID : 441009723609 Option 3 ID : 441009723606 Option 4 ID : 441009723608 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 62, "q": "What laboratory test is used to monitor disease progression and immune status in HIV- positive patients? Ans 1. CD4+ T cell count 2. Liver function tests 3. HIV viral load 4. Complete blood count Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160745 Option 1 ID : 441009636743 Option 2 ID : 441009636745 Option 3 ID : 441009636742 Option 4 ID : 441009636744 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 63, "q": "The pH range that supports optimal growth for most bacteria is _________. Ans 1. 2.5-3.5 2. 3.2-6.2 3. 4.2-5.2 4. 7.2-7.6 Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009160118 Option 1 ID : 441009634770 Option 2 ID : 441009634772 Option 3 ID : 441009634771 Option 4 ID : 441009634773 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 4", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 64, "q": "In placenta previa, due to repeated small bouts of hemorrhage while carrying on the expectant treatment can cause chronic placental insufficiency leads to_________. Ans 1. fetal growth restriction 2. intrauterine death 3. asphyxia 4. congenital malformation Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009162696 Option 1 ID : 441009644436 Option 2 ID : 441009644438 Option 3 ID : 441009644437 Option 4 ID : 441009644439 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 65, "q": "The average increase in the head circumference of an infant from birth to 3 months is: Ans 1. 1.5 cm/month 2. 1 cm/month 3. 0.5 cm/month 4. 2 cm/month Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009185241 Option 1 ID : 441009732299 Option 2 ID : 441009732300 Option 3 ID : 441009732301 Option 4 ID : 441009732298 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 3", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 66, "q": "Foods rich in carbohydrates and fats are called as Ans 1. Body building 2. Protective 3. Energy yielding 4. Regulatory Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009174009 Option 1 ID : 441009688452 Option 2 ID : 441009688454 Option 3 ID : 441009688453 Option 4 ID : 441009688455 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 67, "q": "Role of Indian Nursing Council in nursing profession is--------. Ans 1. to regulate nursing programme 2. to provide nursing registration 3. to conduct nursing examination 4. to provide job to nurses Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009162256 Option 1 ID : 441009642677 Option 2 ID : 441009642680 Option 3 ID : 441009642678 Option 4 ID : 441009642679 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 2", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 68, "q": "The system of differentiations which includes a hierarchy of social positions are termed as, Ans 1. Social class 2. social caste 3. social mobility 4. Social stratification Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009180783 Option 1 ID : 441009714444 Option 2 ID : 441009714446 Option 3 ID : 441009714445 Option 4 ID : 441009714443 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 69, "q": "In which brain tumor, there is presence of multiple deposits, well defined and usually located at the grey and white matter junction? Ans 1. Ependymoma 2. Metastatic brain tumor 3. Medulloblastoma 4. Oligodendroglioma Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009162386 Option 1 ID : 441009643198 Option 2 ID : 441009643197 Option 3 ID : 441009643196 Option 4 ID : 441009643199 Status : Not Answered Chosen Option : --", "o": [], "a": null}, {"n": 70, "q": "Lymph nodes found in the chest, near the lungs and heart, are called as----------. Ans 1. Mediastinal lymph nodes 2. Cervical lymph nodes 3. Popliteal lymph nodes 4. Inguinal lymph nodes Question Type : MCQ Question ID : 441009159684 Option 1 ID : 441009633555 Option 2 ID : 441009633557 Option 3 ID : 441009633556 Option 4 ID : 441009633554 Status : Answered Chosen Option : 1", "o": [], "a": null}]});

