window.PYQ_OCR['sbi-po'].push({t:'sbi po 2023 prelims',q:[{"n": 1, "q": "Directions: Each of the following sentences has a blank space and five words are given below. Click on the word you consider the most APPROPRIATE to fit the blank. A special team was formed to _______ the lost fisherman who was stranded on the freezing lake after dark.", "o": [". Rescue", ". Unpleasant", ". Meditate", ". Speculate 5. Revenue"], "a": 0}, {"n": 2, "q": "Directions: Each of the following sentences has a blank space and five words are given below. Click on the word you consider the most APPROPRIATE to fit the blank. If the media continues to _______ young black men as thugs and gangsters, the stereotype will continue to persist in society.", "o": [". Betray", ". Deceive", ". Portray", ". Request 5. Console"], "a": 2}, {"n": 3, "q": "Directions: Each of the following sentences has a blank space and five words are given below. Click on the word you consider the most APPROPRIATE to fit the blank. The police were able to _______ the woman’s stolen purse after they caught and arrested the thief who had taken it.", "o": [". Prefer", ". Instruct", ". Refer", ". Obstruct 5. Recover"], "a": 4}, {"n": 4, "q": "Directions: Select the most appropriate word to fill in the blank. The manager urged the team to avoid ________ evaluations and strive for thoroughness.", "o": ["cursory Page 1", "foolishness", "precise", "attentive 5. thorough"], "a": 0}, {"n": 5, "q": "Directions: The given sentence is divided into four parts that are A, B, C, and D. Choose the part that contains an error as your answer. If the sentence is error-free, mark E i.e. No error as your answer. Everyone at the meeting (A) were surprised (B) when the CEO announced (C) his retirement. (D) No error (E)", "o": [". A", ". B", ". C", ". D 5. E"], "a": 1}, {"n": 6, "q": "Directions: The given sentence is divided into four parts that are A, B, C, and D. Choose the part that contains an error as your answer. If the sentence is error-free, mark E i.e. No error as your answer. Running through the park (A), a squirrel caught my attention (B) as it was darting up a tree (C) in search of its nest (D). No Error (E)", "o": [". A", ". D", ". C", ". B 5. E"], "a": 4}, {"n": 7, "q": "Directions: The given sentence is divided into four parts that are A, B, C, and D. Choose the part that contains an error as your answer. If the sentence is error-free, mark E i.e. 'No error' as your answer. As it is to be superior than (A) static graphics, animation is (B) being increasingly employed in (C) technology- based learning resources. (D) No error (E)", "o": [". A", ". B", ". C", ". D 5. E Page"], "a": 0}, {"n": 8, "q": "Directions: The following sentence has been split into five segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error. If there is no error, mark 'No error' as your answer. Most investors would (A)/agree that there is (B)/no silver bullet (C)/for valuation companies.(D)/No error.(E)", "o": [". A", ". B", ". C", ". D 5. E"], "a": 3}, {"n": 9, "q": "Directions: The following sentence has been split into five segments. Identify the segment that contains a grammatical error. If there is no error, mark 'No error' as your answer. Technical innovation in India's (A)/ renewable energy policy (B)/ is deepening a high (C)/ uneven energy landscape (D)/No error. (E)", "o": [". A", ". B", ". C", ". D 5. E"], "a": 2}, {"n": 10, "q": "Directions: The following sentences form a paragraph. The rest of the sentences are marked as A, B, C, D, E and F. Sentence 'C' is in the correct place. The rest of the sentences are not given in their proper order. Read the sentences and answer the following questions. A. Artificial Intelligence refers to the intelligence of machines. B. Most noteworthy, Artificial Intelligence is the simulation of human intelligence by machines. C. With Artificial Intelligence, machines perform functions such as learning, planning, reasoning and problem-solving. D. Furthermore, many experts believe AI could solve major challenges and crisis situations. E. This is in contrast to the natural intelligence of humans and animals. F. It is probably the fastest-growing development in the World of technology and innovation. Which sentence should be the SECOND sentence in the paragraph?", "o": [". D", ". A", ". F", ". E 5. B Page"], "a": 3}, {"n": 11, "q": "Which sentence should be the FOURTH sentence in the paragraph?", "o": [". F", ". A", ". B", ". D 5. E"], "a": 2}, {"n": 12, "q": "Which sentence should be the SIXTH sentence in the paragraph?", "o": [". D", ". E", ". F", ". B 5. A"], "a": 0}, {"n": 13, "q": "Which sentence should be the FIRST sentence in the paragraph?", "o": [". D", ". A", ". B", ". E 5. F"], "a": 1}, {"n": 14, "q": "Which sentence should be the FIFTH sentence in the paragraph?", "o": [". E", ". D", ". A", ". B 5. F"], "a": 4}, {"n": 15, "q": "Directions: In the following question, the given table has two columns (I and II) containing three phrases each. The phrases are labelled A, B, and C in the first column and P, Q, and R in the second column. A phrase from the first column may or may not connect with a phrase in the second column to make a grammatically and contextually meaningful sentence. Identify the correct option given Page 4 below that gives the correct sequence in which one or more sentences can be formed. If none of the options make a meaningful sentence, mark 'None of these' as your answer. Column I Column II (A) Sophie was born in France, but (P) result in a greater reduction in shortly thereafter employee numbers than we had. (B) The recession blindsided a lot of (Q) taken for granted their lawyers who had previously comfortable income. (C) About 23% of men and women (R) her family moved to the United aged 25 to 34 told researchers States.", "o": ["C-Q and B-P", "A-Q", "A-R and B-Q", "C-P 5. None of these"], "a": 2}, {"n": 16, "q": "Directions: In the following question, the given table has two columns (I and II) containing three phrases each. The phrases are labelled A, B, and C in the first column and P, Q, and R in the second column. A phrase from the first column may or may not connect with a phrase in the second column to make a grammatically and contextually meaningful sentence. Identify the correct option given below that gives the correct sequence in which one or more sentences can be formed. If none of the options make a meaningful sentence, mark 'None of these' as your answer. Column I Column II (A) You can hear people fall about (P) conversant with basic scientific laughing principles. (B) Those in business are not, on the (Q) once in a while to avoid product whole, build-up. (C) I think you should change your (R) even if you are dieting, you can shampoo and conditioner indulge yourself.", "o": [". B-Q", ". B-P and C-Q", ". C-P and A-Q", ". A-R 5. None of these"], "a": 1}, {"n": 17, "q": "Directions: In the following question, the given table has two columns (I and II) containing three phrases each. The phrases are labelled A, B, and C in the first column and P, Q, and R in the second column. A phrase from the first column may or may not connect with a phrase in the second column to make a grammatically and contextually meaningful sentence. Identify the correct option given below that gives the correct sequence in which one or more sentences can be formed. If none of the options make a meaningful sentence, mark 'None of these' as your answer. Column I Column II Page 5 (A) We suspect they are trying to hide (P) members of some group something, hence within society. (B) The amount of Business Rate each (Q) we suspect they are trying to local authority receives will bear hide something (C) He was jailed for 33 months to run (R) with a sentence he is already concurrently serving for burglary.", "o": ["A-P", "B-Q", "A-Q and B-R", "C-R 5. None of these"], "a": 3}, {"n": 18, "q": "Directions: In the following question, the given table has two columns (I and II) containing three phrases each. The phrases are labelled A, B, and C in the first column and P, Q, and R in the second column. A phrase from the first column may or may not connect with a phrase in the second column to make a grammatically and contextually meaningful sentence. Identify the correct option given below that gives the correct sequence in which one or more sentences can be formed. If none of the options make a meaningful sentence, mark 'None of these' as your answer. Column I Column II (A) Occasionally, primary (P) evidently just come from the hyperparathyroidism has been known to bathroom. (B) On the contrary, the project will (Q) with the regular legislative produce valuable reference session beginning today. (R) material and should be lauded (C) The man wore a bathrobe and had for its novelty and foresight.", "o": [". A-Q", ". C-R and A-P", ". B-R and C-P", ". C-Q 5. None of these"], "a": 2}, {"n": 19, "q": "Direction: Select the phrase from the options below that should replace the underlined phrase in the sentence to make it grammatically and contextually correct. If the sentence is already correct, select 'No correction required' as your answer. His behaviour with all his employees is so pleasing that everyone come forward for helping him.", "o": [". came towards him for help", ". comes towards him for help", ". comes forward to help him", ". comes forward for help him 5. no correction required Page 6"], "a": 2}, {"n": 20, "q": "Direction: Select the phrase from the options below that should replace the underlined phrase in the sentence to make it grammatically and contextually correct. If the sentence is already correct, select 'No correction required' as your answer. The police commissioner burst into rage and ordered immediately suspension of the inspector.", "o": [". order immediately", ". order immediate", ". ordered immediate", ". ordering immediate 5. no correction required"], "a": 2}, {"n": 21, "q": "Directions: Select the phrase from the options below that should replace the underlined phrase in the sentence to make it grammatically and contextually correct. If the sentence is already correct, select 'No correction required' as your answer. Sub-zero temperatures throughout most of the Europe is increasing demand for gas, and several governments have issued calls for conservation.", "o": [". most of Europe were increased", ". most of Europe are increasing", ". much of the Europe is increasing", ". much of Europe have been increasing 5. No correction required"], "a": 1}, {"n": 22, "q": "Directions: Read the given passage carefully to answer the following questions. Each question will have five alternatives as its answer. Choose the correct option as your answer. In the evolving landscape of financial education, a new category of educators has emerged—financial advisory influencers. These individuals leverage social media platforms to disseminate knowledge and advice on various financial topics. Their expertise ranges from basic budgeting techniques to complex investment strategies, making finance more accessible to the general populace. The influence of these financial gurus is substantial. They simplify the esoteric world of finance, which often seems intimidating to the uninitiated. By breaking down complex concepts into digestible chunks, they empower individuals to make informed decisions about their money. This democratization of financial knowledge is crucial in an era where economic literacy is paramount. Moreover, financial advisory influencers often tailor their content to cater to diverse audiences. Whether it's a college student looking to manage student loans or a retiree planning their estate, there's something valuable for everyone. Their approachable style and practical advice have garnered them millions of followers who tune in for their insights and tips. However, the rise of these influencers also presents challenges. The accuracy of the information they provide can vary, and their recommendations might not always be tailored to individual needs. Thus, while they play a pivotal role in financial education, it's essential for consumers to critically evaluate the advice given and consider consulting professional financial advisors for personalized guidance. Page 7 In summary, financial advisory influencers have transformed the way financial knowledge is consumed and understood. They serve as a bridge between the complex world of finance and the average person, contributing significantly to financial literacy. Nevertheless, the onus remains on the individual to verify the credibility of the information and adapt it to their personal financial situation. What is a synonym for \"disseminate\" as used in the passage?", "o": [". conceal", ". distribute", ". withhold", ". hide 5. cover"], "a": 1}, {"n": 23, "q": "What is a synonym for \"empower\" as mentioned in the passage?", "o": [". weaken", ". enable", ". prevent", ". prohibit 5. disable"], "a": 1}, {"n": 24, "q": "Which of the following statements is true based on the passage? A) Financial advisory influencers primarily focus on selling their financial products. B) Financial advisory influencers simplify complex financial concepts for the general public. C) All financial advisory influencers provide legally binding financial advice", "o": [". Only A", ". Only B", ". Only C", ". Both A & B 5. None of the above"], "a": 1}, {"n": 25, "q": "What is the primary role of financial advisory influencers according to the passage?", "o": [". To promote their own financial products.", ". To simplify complex financial concepts for the general public.", ". To provide legally binding financial advice.", ". To replace professional financial advisors. 5. To focus solely on wealthy clients. Page 8"], "a": 1}, {"n": 26, "q": "Which of the following is NOT presented as a challenge associated with financial advisory influencers?", "o": [". Variability in the accuracy of the information provided.", ". Their inability to reach a wide audience.", ". Their recommendations may not be tailored to individual needs.", ". The potential for consumers to misinterpret the advice. 5. Over-reliance on social media platforms for dissemination."], "a": 1}, {"n": 27, "q": "What is an antonym for \"complex\" as used in the passage?", "o": [". intricate", ". complicated", ". difficult", ". simple 5. convoluted"], "a": 3}, {"n": 28, "q": "Based on the passage, why is it crucial for consumers to critically evaluate the advice provided by financial advisory influencers?", "o": [". Because the influencers often charge high fees for their services.", ". Because the influencers' advice can be biased towards certain financial products.", ". Because the advice might not always be accurate or suitable for everyone.", ". Because all financial influencers have a background in financial law. 5. Because influencers are legally responsible for the financial outcomes of their followers."], "a": 2}, {"n": 29, "q": "In the given sentence a word has been emboldened. Select the best alternative for the bold word from the given options. If none follows, select option 5 as your answer. Adrian expected Alyssa to resent him for his actions.", "o": [". Admire", ". Agree", ". Dislike", ". Welcome 5. None of these"], "a": 2}, {"n": 30, "q": "In the given sentence a word has been emboldened. Select the best alternative for the bold word from the given options. If none follows, select option 5 as your answer. Page 9 Marissa was disappointed by her son's behaviour.", "o": [". Riled up", ". Let down", ". Let go", ". Give up 5. None of these"], "a": 1}, {"n": 31, "q": "Directions: The given pie chart 1 shows the percentage distribution of the number of persons (Male + Female) visited park in five different days Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday and Friday. Total number of persons (Male + Female) = 1500 Pie chart 2 shows the percentage distribution of the number of males visiting the park on five different days Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday and Friday. Total number of males visiting park = 800 Page 10 On Monday the number of males visited park in FN is 3/5 th out of total males visited and the rest of remaining visited AN. If the number of males visited FN have two wheelers and half of the males visited AN have four wheelers and remaining have two wheelers. Find the number of males having two wheelers visited on Monday.", "o": ["84", "92", "96", "98 5. 102"], "a": 2}, {"n": 32, "q": "Number of females visited park on Saturday is 20% more than the number of females visited park on Monday. Out of total visited females on saturday 3/5 th of them are married then find the number of unmarried females visited park on saturday is what percentage of the total visited females on all five days.", "o": ["13.89%", "12.34%", "15.64%", "10.28% 5. 21.89%"], "a": 3}, {"n": 33, "q": "Find the difference between the number of males visited the park on Tuesday and Thursday and the number of female visited on Monday and Wednesday.", "o": ["30", "25", "10", "15 5. 20"], "a": 2}, {"n": 34, "q": "If 1/3rd and 2/3rd of males visiting parks on Monday and Friday are below 30, the rest of them are above 30. If the total number of persons (Male + Female) whose age is above 30 visiting parks is 250. Find total females visiting the park age above 30.", "o": ["140", "130", "120", "90 5. 110 Page 11"], "a": 4}, {"n": 35, "q": "Find the ratio between the number of males visiting the park on Tuesday and Wednesday to the number of females visiting the park on Thursday and Friday.", "o": ["12: 17", "13: 19", "13: 11", "15: 17 5. 18: 11"], "a": 4}, {"n": 36, "q": "The average weight of 20 contestants in a fashion show increased by 5.75 kg when one of the contestants left the show but when a new contestant joined the show then the average weight decreased by 2.75 kg. What is the difference between the weight of the new contestant who joined the show and the contestant who left the show?", "o": ["55.5 kg", "49.75 kg", "51.5 kg", "Cannot be determined 5. None of the above"], "a": 2}, {"n": 37, "q": "Mitul goes out to shop on a snowy day. He travels at a speed of a km/hr when it’s snowing and at 'a' speed of (a – 1) km/hr when it stops snowing. If his average speed for the journey is 6.4 km/hr. Find the fraction of the distance which he covered while it was snowing. Given, that 'a' is an integer.", "o": ["7/15", "7/16", "1/4", "3/5 5. None of the above"], "a": 1}, {"n": 38, "q": "What should come in place of the question mark '?' in the following number series? 12, 5.5, 6.5, 11, ?, 376", "o": ["49", "48", "42", "53 5. None of these Page 12"], "a": 1}, {"n": 39, "q": "What should come in place of the question mark '?' in the following number series? 930, 812, 506, ?, 272, 156", "o": ["450", "342", "225", "345 5. 375"], "a": 1}, {"n": 40, "q": "What should come in place of the question mark '?' in the following number series? 6000, ?, 3000, 4500, 9000, 22500", "o": ["2000", "1500", "3500", "3000 5. 2500"], "a": 3}, {"n": 41, "q": "What should come in place of the question mark '?' in the following number series? 1512, 1524, 1540, 1563, ?, 1642", "o": ["1525", "1524", "1528", "1427 5. 1596"], "a": 4}, {"n": 42, "q": "What will come in the place of question mark in the following number series ? 290 , ? , 374 , 421 , 474 , 533", "o": ["341", "331", "351", "347 5. 337"], "a": 1}, {"n": 43, "q": "The interest received on a certain sum of money at 20% per annum compounded annually for 2 years is Rs. 4,600 more than compounded half yearly for 1 year. Find the sum of money. Page 13", "o": ["Rs. 20,000", "Rs. 32,000", "Rs. 50,000", "Rs. 47,000 5. Rs. 40,000"], "a": 0}, {"n": 44, "q": "Three bags whose volumes are in the ratio of 3 : 5 : 7 are full of lime and silica. In the 1st bag the ratio of lime and silica is 5 : 1, in 2nd bag the ratio is 7 : 3 and in the 3rd bag the ratio is 3 : 4. All the three mixtures are mixed in another bag. Find the ratio of lime and silica in the final mixture.", "o": ["4:3", "3:2", "3:4", "2:3 5. 2:1"], "a": 1}, {"n": 45, "q": "Directions : Table given below shows the total population (male + female) in four different villages and the percentage of females out of total population in each of the villages . Total population in all the villages together is 15400. Villages Total Population Percentage of females A 2400 (50 - X)% B 5500 (19.5 + X)% C 280X 40.2% D 32000 of X% 30% Out of total males in village D 28.57% of them are graduated and the rest are non graduated out of total graduated males 40% of them are job workers then find the difference between number of male job workers in village D and the number of non graduated males in the same village.", "o": ["1270", "1440", "1540", "1680 5. 1260 Page 14"], "a": 3}, {"n": 46, "q": "If the number of females in village E is X% more than that in village B, then find the average number of females in village E and A together.", "o": ["1680", "1280", "1440", "1320 5. 1760"], "a": 2}, {"n": 47, "q": "Find the difference between the total number of males in Village B and Village C and total number of females in Village A and B", "o": ["4237", "2127", "3889", "3173 5. 3457"], "a": 3}, {"n": 48, "q": "Total number of females in village D is 75% of the number of females in village F and the average number of males and females in village F is 1700. Find the number of males in the village F.", "o": ["1850", "1700", "1600", "1800 5. 1750"], "a": 3}, {"n": 49, "q": "If 1/5 th of males in village B and 1/3 rd of the females in village A are married then find the ratio between the number of unmarried females in village A to the number of unmarried males in village B.", "o": ["97: 78", "121: 154", "129: 157", "75 : 374 5. 101: 147"], "a": 3}, {"n": 50, "q": "A and B entered into a business such that the sum invested by A is 2/5th of the total sum invested by both of them and A invested his sum for 8 months. The profit received by B is 3/7th of total profit received by A and B together. Find the time for which B invested his sum? Page 15", "o": ["8 months", "4 months", "6 months", "12 months 5. None of these"], "a": 1}, {"n": 51, "q": "P alone can finish the work in 15 hours and Q alone can finish the work in 20 hours while R alone can finish the work in N hours. All three worked for 5 hours, after that P left the work and remaining work gets completed in 3 hours. Find the value of N.", "o": ["20", "30", "25", "24 5. 12"], "a": 1}, {"n": 52, "q": "The hemispherical pot of surface area 882π sq.cm is fulled with milk. The all milk is poured into the cylindrical can of same radius. The cylindrical can is completely filled with milk. Find the height of cylindrical can.", "o": ["16cm", "18cm", "14cm", "21cm 5. 7cm"], "a": 2}, {"n": 53, "q": "What approximate value should come in the place of question mark (?) in the following question? 14.972 × 4.99 ÷ 44.78 + 299.99 ÷ √5624.98 × 12.93 = ?", "o": ["71", "68", "77", "70 5. None of These"], "a": 2}, {"n": 54, "q": "What approximate value will come in the place of the question mark '?' in the following question? {12960.31 ÷ 79.79 × (9.75)2} ÷ 89.89 + √195.79 - 10.23 = ? Page 16", "o": ["184", "162", "204", "211 5. 193"], "a": 0}, {"n": 55, "q": "What approximate value will come in the place of the question mark '?' in the following question? 14.66 × 22.28 - 344.81 ÷ 23.38 + (11.73)2 - 68.87 = ?", "o": ["415", "270", "331", "390 5. 175"], "a": 3}, {"n": 56, "q": "What approximate will come in the place of the question mark ‘?’ in the following question? 37.98% of 549.99 + √(49.02) ÷ ? = 7.99 × (2.97)3", "o": ["0", "1", "2", "3 5. 4"], "a": 1}, {"n": 57, "q": "What approximate will come in the place of the question mark ‘?’ in the following question? 9.78% of 79.94 + ?% of 9.67 = 10.94 × 2.99 + √100 × 2.98", "o": ["600", "550", "580", "610 5. None of these."], "a": 1}, {"n": 58, "q": "Directions: Two quantities I and II are given in the following questions. You have to find the value to both I and II by using your knowledge of mathematics and choose the most suitable relation between the magnitude of I and II from the given options. Page 17 Quantity I: On a mask SP is 425% more than the cost price. If cost price is increased by 5% then calculate new profit margin in percentage if selling price of mask remain the same. Quantity II: A company is offering 80% discount on the marked price because of which selling price is equal to cost price. Calculate percentage mark up.", "o": ["Quantity I ≥ Quantity II", "Quantity I ≤ Quantity II", "Quantity I > Quantity II", "Quantity I = Quantity II 5. Quantity I< Quantity II"], "a": 3}, {"n": 59, "q": "Given below are two quantities named A and B. Based on the given information, you have to determine the relationship between the two quantities. You should use the given data and your knowledge of Mathematics to choose between the possible answers. Quantity A: A task of painting a house is given to A and B for Rs. 15000, with the help of C the task is completed in 6 days. had A alone done the task he would take 12 days. Had B alone done the task he would take 15 days. Find the share of C in the money given for the task? Quantity B: Rs 1500", "o": ["Quantity A > Quantity B", "Quantity A < Quantity B", "Quantity A ≥ Quantity B", "Quantity A ≤ Quantity B 5. Quantity A = Quantity B or No relation"], "a": 4}, {"n": 60, "q": "Given below are two quantities named A and B. Based on the given information, you have to determine the relationship between the two quantities. You should use the given data and your knowledge of Mathematics to choose between the possible answers. Quantity A: In a 63 liters mixture of alcohol and water, the ratio of alcohol to water is 5 : 4. In order to make the ratio of alcohol to water 3 : 2, some quantity of alcohol is to be added to the mixture. The quantity of alcohol present in the new mixture is? Quantity B: 43 l", "o": ["Quantity A > Quantity B", "Quantity A < Quantity B", "Quantity A ≥ Quantity B", "Quantity A ≤ Quantity B 5. Quantity A = Quantity B or No relation"], "a": 1}, {"n": 61, "q": "In the question, two quantities I and II are given. You have to solve both the quantities and establish the correct relation between Quantity - I and Quantity - II and choose the correct Page 18 option accordingly. Quantity I: Difference between the ages of Yash and Kush is 6 years. Three years later, the sum of their ages will be 40 years. How old was Yash 4 years ago? Quantity II: Two years later, Viru's age will be two - third of Veer's age at that time. Sum of their present ages is 26 years. What is the present age of Viru?", "o": ["Quantity - I < Quantity - II", "Quantity - I > Quantity - II", "Quantity - I ≥ Quantity - II", "Quantity - I ≤ Quantity - II 5. Quantity - I =Quantity - II or No relation"], "a": 2}, {"n": 62, "q": "There are three voting booths in a city. The number of voters in the first two booths is 52% and 46% of the third booth. The difference in the number of voters in the first booth and second booth is 7686, then find the total number of voters in all three booths.", "o": ["2,53,648", "2,53,658", "2,53,638", "2,53,668 5. None of these"], "a": 2}, {"n": 63, "q": "Amir bought the article at a discount of 20% on the Marked price and then He sold the article with a 10% loss on the cost price.What would have been the percentage loss had he bought it at the marked price?", "o": ["36%", "40%", "28%", "46% 5. None of the above."], "a": 2}, {"n": 64, "q": "Ramiya got married 8 years ago. Her present age is 6/5 times her age at the time of her marriage. Ramiya’s brother was 10 years younger than her at the time of her marriage. What is the ratio of Ramiya’s present age and her brother’s age at the time of her marriage?", "o": ["2:7", "7:9", "4:7", "8:5 Page 19 5. None of the above"], "a": 3}, {"n": 65, "q": "Two boats X and Y start towards each other from two different places, 300 km apart. The speed of the boat X and Y in still water are 8 km/hr and 7 km/hr respectively. If X proceeds down and Y up the stream, they will meet after.", "o": ["25 hours", "20 hours", "15 hours", "5 hours 5. 10 hours"], "a": 1}, {"n": 66, "q": "Direction: Read the following information carefully and answer the given questions. Ten persons Lata, Uma, Gia, Sana, Tia, Pia, Kate, Hina, Noor, and Ruhi were born in ten different months January, March, April, May, June, July, August, September, October, and December but not necessarily in same order. Tia was born in the month which has 30 days before August. Only four persons were born between Tia and Sana. Uma was born just before Sana. The number of persons born before Uma and after Noor are equal. Gia was born in a month which has 30 days only. Only one person was born between Ruhi and Lata. Ruhi was born before Lata. Only three persons were born between Pia and Gia. Pia was born before Gia. Less than three people were born between Lata and Hina. In which month Noor is born?", "o": ["March", "January", "December", "October 5. July"], "a": 0}, {"n": 67, "q": "Who is born just after Pia is born?", "o": [". the one who is born in the month of September.", ". Sana", ". the one who is born in the month of June.", ". Hina 5. the one who is born in the month of March."], "a": 2}, {"n": 68, "q": "How many persons are born between Gia and Hina? Page 20", "o": ["Five", "Two", "Seven", "Eight 5. One"], "a": 4}, {"n": 69, "q": "Which of the following statement is/are true?", "o": ["Lata was born in April.", "Pia was born before Sana.", "Noor is born in the month which has 30 days.", "Both 1 and 2 5. Both 2 and 3"], "a": 3}, {"n": 70, "q": "Which among the following combination is true?", "o": [". June-Gia", ". October-Hina", ". August-Kate", ". January-Pia 5. March-Lata"], "a": 2}, {"n": 71, "q": "Direction: In the question below are given three statements followed by two conclusions numbered I and II. You have to take the given statements to be true even if they seem to be at variance with commonly known facts. Read all the conclusions and then decide which of the given conclusions logically follows from the given statements disregarding commonly known facts. Statements: Some story are real. All fake are news. No fake is real. Conclusions: I) Some story are not fake. II) Some story can be fake.", "o": ["Only conclusion I follows", "Only conclusion II follows Page 21", "Either conclusion I or II follows", "Neither conclusion I nor II follows 5. Both conclusion I and II follows"], "a": 4}, {"n": 72, "q": "Direction: In the question below are given three statements followed by three conclusions I and II. You have to take the given statements to be true even if they seem to be at variance from commonly known facts, Read all the given conclusions and then decide which of the following conclusions logically follows from the given statements disregarding commonly known facts. Statements: Some door are fan. No door is rose. No fan is shelf. Conclusions: (I) All doors are shelf is a possibility. (II) All shelf can be door.", "o": [". Only conclusion I follows", ". Only conclusion II follows", ". Both conclusion I and II follows", ". Neither conclusion I nor II follows 5. Either conclusion I or II follows"], "a": 1}, {"n": 73, "q": "Direction: In the question below are given three statements followed by two conclusions numbered I and II. You have to take the given statements to be true even if they seem to be at variance with commonly known facts. Read all the conclusions and then decide which of the given conclusions logically follows from the given statements disregarding commonly known facts. Statements: No sad is laugh. No joy is sad. No sorrow is joy. Conclusions: I. Some sad can be sorrow. II. Some laugh is joy.", "o": ["Only I follows", "Neither I nor II follows", "Only II follows Page 22", "Either I or II follows 5. Both I and II follow"], "a": 0}, {"n": 74, "q": "Direction: Read the following information carefully and answer the given questions. Six boxes U, V, W, X, Y, and Z have different colors Maroon, Ivory, Purple, Lavender, Blush, and Aqua. The boxes are placed one above the other but not necessarily in the same order. Two boxes are there between the Ivory and Maroon color boxes. The maroon color box is placed below the Ivory color box. Only one box is placed between Box W and the Ivory color box. No box was placed between the Z and Maroon color boxes. Z is not a Maroon color box. The box U was placed just above the lavender color box. Box U is neither an Ivory color nor a Blush color box. Box X is placed below the Lavender color box. Only three boxes were placed between box Y and the Blush color box. Box V is placed below both the Blush and Aqua color boxes. How many boxes are kept between U and Z?", "o": [". One", ". Two", ". Five", ". Three 5. Four"], "a": 1}, {"n": 75, "q": "Which of the box is kept exactly in the middle of the box which has a Maroon color, and the one which has a Purple color?", "o": [". Box Z", ". Box U", ". Box X", ". Box W 5. Box V"], "a": 0}, {"n": 76, "q": "As many boxes are kept above X as below_____.", "o": [". the box which has Blush color.", ". Box U", ". the box which has Maroon color.", ". Box Z 5. the box which is placed immediately below the Aqua color box"], "a": 4}, {"n": 77, "q": "Page 23 If the position of box which has Purple color and Aqua color is interchanged then which of the following box is kept two box below Maroon?", "o": ["Box V", "Box X", "Box Y", "Box U 5. Box Z"], "a": 3}, {"n": 78, "q": "Which of the following box is kept third from the top of the stack?", "o": [". the box which is kept immediately above F.", ". the box which has Ivory color.", ". The one who likes Lavender color.", ". Box U 5. Box Z"], "a": 2}, {"n": 79, "q": "If odd digits in the given number \"286354256\" are increased by three and the even digit of the number is decreased by two, then what is the sum of all the digits of the number thus formed?", "o": ["40", "30", "38", "35 5. 34"], "a": 2}, {"n": 80, "q": "How many pairs of letters are there in the word \"SOMETHING\" each of which has as many letters between them in the word as in the English alphabetical series (both forward and backward direction)?", "o": [". One", ". Two", ". Three", ". More than three 5. None"], "a": 3}, {"n": 81, "q": "Direction: Read the following information carefully and answer the given questions. There are eight members P, Q, R, S, T, U, V, and I in the family. P is the sister of Q. Q and R are married. R and S is the only child of T. S is unmarried. V is the grandmother of U. U is the nephew of S. I is the daughter-in-law of V. Page 24 How is P related to U?", "o": ["Mother", "Father", "Sister", "Wife 5. Aunt"], "a": 4}, {"n": 82, "q": "How is Q related to T?", "o": [". Son or daughter", ". Son", ". Son-in-law", ". daughter-in-law 5. Son-in-law or daughter-in-law"], "a": 4}, {"n": 83, "q": "If K is married to I then what is the relation of K and P?", "o": [". K is the sister of P", ". K is the father of P", ". K is the uncle of P", ". K is the brother of P 5. K is the son of P"], "a": 3}, {"n": 84, "q": "Direction: Read the following information carefully and answer the given questions. Eight persons Varun, Pinku, Kabir, Fane, Avi, Seema, Rohan, and Ena are sitting in the circle some are facing the center and some are facing opposite to the center. Number of person facing center is less than the number of persons facing opposite to the center. Seema is facing the center. Varun sits second to the right of Seema. Two persons sit between Varun and Pinku. Immediate neighbors of Pinku are facing the opposite direction to Pinku. Ena sits second to the left of Pinku. Ena is not an immediate neighbor of Varun. Rohan is not a neighbor of Pinku and Ena. Kabir sits second to the right of Rohan. Avi is not an immediate neighbor of Ena. Who sits to the immediate right of Kabir?", "o": [". Pinku", ". The person who sits to the immediate left of Ena.", ". Avi", ". The person who sits second to right of Rohan 5. Fane Page"], "a": 1}, {"n": 85, "q": "Who sits exactly in between Varun and Fane when counted to the left of Varun?", "o": [". Rohan", ". Ena", ". Pinku", ". Kabir 5. Avi"], "a": 4}, {"n": 86, "q": "Who is sitting fourth to the right of the person who is sitting second to the right of Kabir?", "o": [". Rohan", ". Ena", ". Fane", ". Varun 5. Pinku"], "a": 0}, {"n": 87, "q": "Which of the following statements is false according to the given arrangement? I. Rohan is sitting second to the right of Pinku. II. Kabir and Varun are facing the same direction. III. The immediate neighbor of Avi is facing the same direction as Avi.", "o": [". Only I", ". Both I and II", ". Only II", ". Both II and III 5. Only III"], "a": 4}, {"n": 88, "q": "Four of the following five are alike in a certain way based on the given arrangement and hence form a group. Which of the following does not belong to that group?", "o": [". Rohan", ". Ena", ". Seema", ". Pinku 5. Kabir Page"], "a": 2}, {"n": 89, "q": "Five letter-clusters have been given, out of which four are alike in some manner and one is different. Select the letter-cluster that is different.", "o": [". IRYB", ". LYGJ", ". MGHZ", ". NCPV 5. RYEF"], "a": 3}, {"n": 90, "q": "Directions: In the following question assuming the given statements to be true, find which of the conclusion among the given conclusions is/ are definitely true and then give your answers accordingly Statement: N > F > O ≤ M, O ≤ B > A Conclusion: I) O < A II) M ≤ O", "o": [". Only conclusion I is true", ". Only Conclusion II is true", ". Either conclusion I or II is true", ". Neither conclusion I or II is true 5. Both conclusion I and II is true"], "a": 3}, {"n": 91, "q": "Direction: In the following question, assuming the given statement to be true, find which of the conclusion(s) among the given conclusions is/are definitely true, and then give your answers accordingly. Statement: T < U < X; U < W < Z = O; Z < N > M Conclusions: I. T > M II. X < N", "o": [". Both I and II follow", ". Neither I nor II follows", ". Only Il follows", ". Only I follows 5. Either I or II follows"], "a": 1}, {"n": 92, "q": "Direction: In this question, the relationship between different elements is shown in the statements. The statements are followed by two conclusions, study the conclusion based on the given statements and Page 27 select the appropriate answer. Statements: O ≤ Z > U > L > A; Z ≤ C ≤ N; L < Q Conclusions: I: O < N II: O = N", "o": ["Only conclusion I is true", "Only conclusion II is true", "Both conclusions I and II are true", "Neither conclusion I nor II is true 5. Either conclusion I or II is true"], "a": 4}, {"n": 93, "q": "Direction: Read the following information carefully and answer the given questions. Six friends Jeet, Kia, Amit, Rishu, Mishi, and Nia are seated in a line facing north. They like different types of books like Poetry, Horror, Memoir, Thriller, Biography, and Classics not necessarily in the same order. Jeet is seated immediately right of Mishi who is third to the left of the one who likes Horror books. Mishi and the one who likes Poetry are seated at a gap of one person. Amit is sitting immediately right of the one who likes Poetry books. At least one person is sitting to the left of Mishi. Nia likes Classics books. Mishi and the one who likes Classics books are not immediate neighbors. Jeet and Rishu do not like Memoir books. Rishu does not like Poetry books and is not an immediate neighbor of Nia. The one who likes Thriller books is not sitting at the extreme ends. Who among the following likes Horror Books?", "o": [". Amit", ". Mishi", ". Kia", ". Nia 5. Jeet"], "a": 0}, {"n": 94, "q": "Which of the following person is sitting third to the left of the person who is sitting at the exteme ends?", "o": [". Mishi", ". The one who likes Thriller Books", ". The one who likes Memoir Books", ". Amit 5. The one who likes Classics books"], "a": 1}, {"n": 95, "q": "Immediately between which of the following pairs of people Kia is sitting?", "o": ["Rishu and Mishi Page 28", "Jeet and Rishu", "Nia and the one who likes Horror books", "the one who likes Thriller and the one who likes Biography. 5. Jeet and Amit"], "a": 4}, {"n": 96, "q": "Which of the following statement is true with respect to Rishu?", "o": [". Rishu is sitting second to the right of Jeet.", ". Rishu is not sitting at the extreme end of the row.", ". Rishu is sitting third to the left of Kia.", ". Rishu is immediate neighbor of the one who likes Poetry. 5. Rishu likes Horror Books."], "a": 2}, {"n": 97, "q": "Which book does the person sitting immediately right of Amit likes?", "o": [". Thriller", ". Classics", ". Horror", ". Biography 5. Poetry"], "a": 1}, {"n": 98, "q": "Direction: Read the following information carefully and answer the given questions. Shyam starts walking from point E. After walking 5m in the north direction he reaches point F. From there he turns to the east direction and walks 6m to reach point G. From there he turns to the Southeast direction and walks 4m to reach point H. Then he turns in the east direction and walks 10m to reach point I. Then he starts walking in the north direction and walks 20m to reach point J. Then he turns in the west direction and walks 12m to reach point K. Then he turns Southwest direction and again walks 3m to reach point L. From L he walks 5m west to reach point M. Then he turns to the North and walks 7m to reach point N. Finally, he turned right and reached point O after walking 2m. What is the shortest distance between points J and H?", "o": ["15m", "20√ 5 m", "25m", "30m 5. 10√ 5 m"], "a": 4}, {"n": 99, "q": "Point N is in which direction with respect to point G? Page 29", "o": ["North", "South-West", "North-West", "North-East 5. South-East"], "a": 2}, {"n": 100, "q": "What is the total longest route, travelled by Shyam, from point H to M?", "o": ["53m", "50m", "40m", "43m 5. 47m Page 30"], "a": 1}]});

