window.PYQ_OCR['sbi-po'].push({t:'sbi po 2025 prelims',q:[{"n": 1, "q": "Read the passage given below and then answer the questions given below the passage. The United States recently lifted its long-standing ban on online betting, paving the way for a significant evolution in the realm of digital entertainment and gambling. This decision has sparked a lively debate among policymakers, economists, and the general public. Proponents argue that online betting, including online poker and various sports wagering platforms, will engage users with a new form of recreational activity while potentially generating substantial revenue through taxation. Critics, however, caution against the social vices that may accompany this shift, such as addiction, financial loss, and deteriorating mental health. With the ban removed, states now have the autonomy to regulate and legislate online betting within their jurisdictions. This is expected to lead to a patchwork of regulations across the country, potentially complicating enforcement and compliance efforts. Moreover, the explosion of online betting activities has raised concerns about the integrity of sports. There is a looming threat that the financial stakes involved in betting might result in increased instances of match-fixing and other unethical practices, compromising the essence of fair sportsmanship. Comparing the situation in the US to Europe, where online betting has long been legal, reveals significant insights. European countries have developed _____________ and control online betting activities, aiming to mitigate the negative impacts while capitalizing on the economic benefits. The US, on the other hand, must now navigate these challenges and learn from Europe’s experiences to create a balanced approach. The impact of this policy change extends to various sectors of society. On one hand, enthusiasts believe that online betting can engage a younger demographic, furnishing them with new avenues for excitement and entertainment. On the other hand, mental health experts warn about the potential vices associated with excessive gambling, including addiction, depression, and financial ruin. It remains to be seen how the US will address these challenges and ensure that the transition to legalized online betting is both economically beneficial and socially responsible. According to the passage, what potential negative impact of online betting is mentioned?", "o": [". Loss of personal privacy", ". Increased risk of addiction", ". Reduction in sports popularity", ". Decrease in state revenue 5. Higher taxes on other forms of entertainment"], "a": 1}, {"n": 2, "q": "Which of the following is a reason cited by proponents for lifting the online betting ban?", "o": [". To increase tourism", ". To reduce crime rates", ". To engage users with a new form of recreational activity", ". To decrease the unemployment rate 5. To promote traditional sports"], "a": 2}, {"n": 3, "q": "According to the passage, who now has the autonomy to regulate and legislate online betting within their jurisdictions?", "o": [". Federal government", ". All betting companies", ". Individual states", ". International bodies 5. The Supreme Court"], "a": 2}, {"n": 4, "q": "Which of the following is expected to result from states having autonomy to regulate online betting within their jurisdictions?", "o": [". A unified national regulation standard", ". Simplified enforcement and compliance efforts", ". The end of match-fixing concerns", ". A patchwork of regulations across the country 5. An immediate increase in sports viewership"], "a": 3}, {"n": 5, "q": "According to the passage, which of the given statements is correct? A) The ban on online betting in the US was removed due to pressure from international sports organizations. B) Critics warn that the removal of the ban may lead to financial ruin for some individuals. C) The US has significant experience in regulating online betting activities compared to European countries.", "o": [". Only A", ". Only B", ". Only C", ". A and B 5. B and C"], "a": 1}, {"n": 6, "q": "It can be inferred from the passage that:", "o": [". Online betting has the potential to generate uneven economic benefits across different states.", ". Sports organizations fully support the lifting of the online betting ban in the US.", ". There will be a uniform response from all states regarding online betting regulations.", ". The majority of Americans are likely to oppose the introduction of online betting. 5. The challenges faced by European countries in online betting are identical to those faced by the US."], "a": 0}, {"n": 7, "q": "What will fit in the blank taken from the passage: “European countries have developed _____________ and control online betting activities, aiming to mitigate the negative impacts while capitalizing on the economic benefits.”", "o": [". Stringent taxation policies", ". Severe penalties", ". Cutting-edge technology", ". Robust regulatory frameworks to monitor 5. Comprehensive advertising strategies"], "a": 3}, {"n": 8, "q": "Which of the following words is similar in meaning to \"engage\" in the context of the passage?", "o": [". Detach", ". Entice", ". Ignore", ". Separate 5. Neglect"], "a": 1}, {"n": 9, "q": "Which of the following words is opposite in meaning to \"vice\" in the context of the passage?", "o": [". Crime", ". Sin", ". Virtue", ". Corruption 5. Depravity"], "a": 2}, {"n": 10, "q": "Direction: The given sentence is divided into four parts: A, B, C, and D. Choose the part that contains an error as your answer. If the sentence is error-free, mark E i.e. No error as your answer. Despite their differing (A) viewpoints on the matter, (B) the team of experts were (C) able to reach an agreement. (D) No error (E)", "o": [". A", ". B", ". C", ". D 5. E"], "a": 2}, {"n": 11, "q": "Direction: The given sentence is divided into four parts: A, B, C, and D. Choose the part that contains an error as your answer. If the sentence is error-free, mark E i.e. No error as your answer. She will finish (A) her degree next year, (B) and then she is applying (C) for her dream job. (D) No error (E)", "o": [". A", ". B", ". C", ". D 5. E"], "a": 2}, {"n": 12, "q": "Direction: The given sentence is divided into four parts: A, B, C, and D. Choose the part that contains an error as your answer. If the sentence is error-free, mark E i.e. No error as your answer. When he was arriving (A) at the party last night, (B) she said she loved the gift, (C) but now she regrets it deeply. (D) No error (E)", "o": [". A", ". B", ". C", ". D 5. E"], "a": 0}, {"n": 13, "q": "Direction: The given sentence is divided into four parts: A, B, C, and D. Choose the part that contains an error as your answer. If the sentence is error-free, mark E i.e. No error as your answer. If I will win the lottery, (A) I will buy a new car, (B) travel the world, (C) and live in luxury. (D) No error (E)", "o": [". A", ". B", ". C", ". D 5. E"], "a": 0}, {"n": 14, "q": "Direction: The given sentence is divided into four parts: A, B, C, and D. Choose the part that contains an error as your answer. If the sentence is error-free, mark E i.e. No error as your answer. Constant exposure to noise (A) can cause increased stress levels, (B) anxiety, irritability, (C) and cognitive impairment. (D) No error (E)", "o": [". A", ". B", ". C", ". D 5. E"], "a": 4}, {"n": 15, "q": "Direction: The given sentence is divided into four parts: A, B, C, and D. Choose the part that contains an error as your answer. If the sentence is error-free, mark E i.e. No error as your answer. Saffron is one of the (A) most expensive spice worldwide, (B) it is valued for its (C) culinary and medicinal value. (D) No error (E)", "o": [". A", ". B", ". C", ". D 5. E"], "a": 1}, {"n": 16, "q": "Direction: The given sentence is divided into four parts: A, B, C, and D. Choose the part that contains an error as your answer. If the sentence is error-free, mark E i.e. No error as your answer. These are just small (A)/ alterations with our lifestyle (B)/ that will help us achieve (C)/ that perfect body. (D)/ No error (E)", "o": [". A", ". B", ". C", ". D 5. E"], "a": 1}, {"n": 17, "q": "Match the statement/s from column 1 with column 2 and find which of the following pairs of statements given in the options make/s contextually and grammatically correct sense. Column 1 Column 2 A. The latest summit D. For the stalled among the USA and negotiations on the North Korea will be a nuclear programme of litmus test North Korea B. Concrete steps to implement the E. The institution was Panmunjom Declaration, sanctioned by named after the border village C. The U.N. Security Council last year as a F. This week's summit part of global efforts is intended to craft", "o": ["Only D-B, E-C and F-A", "Only C-D and B-F", "Only A-D and F-B", "Only D-B, C-E and F-A 5. Only E-C and F-B"], "a": 4}, {"n": 18, "q": "Directions: In the following passage, some words have been deleted. Select the most appropriate option to fill in each blank. I thought kindness as an instinct was worth writing about, considering the lack of sympathy and courtesy one encounters several times a day. Are we, as a society, ___(1)___ public rudeness? People even want to overtake you in a queue while boarding a flight on which everyone’s seat is assured! As you collect a precariously balanced tray of snacks or coffee, a brash neighbour cannot wait 10 seconds for hers; she thinks nothing of jostling your arm or stepping on your foot. So much so, that a polite word from a stranger or a show of ___(2)___ in a supermarket comes as a pleasant shock! This insensitivity to others, deepened by self- preoccupation, is a symptom of a dangerous lack of ___(3)___ kindness. Earphones and mobile screens shut out the world, while users move like robots, oblivious of their fellow humans. Not a moment can be spared for the person seated inches away, perhaps a first-time traveller struggling with a seat belt! Whether plain old-fashioned kindness, a golden ___(4)___? One might call it the gift of caring enough, either when approached for help or sometimes even before one is asked. Often it takes courage to be kind because with it goes the risk of being rejected, perhaps even cheated when you let your guard down to assist another person out of sheer goodwill or ___(5)___. Much safer to do and say nothing? To stay uninvolved? Of course. But if it were to happen to you? If you needed help and people walked by with eyes ___(6)___…what then? Which of the following is the most appropriate option to fill in the blank labelled as (1)?", "o": ["denouncing", "rejecting", "repelling", "condoning 5. enhancing"], "a": 3}, {"n": 19, "q": "Which of the following is the most appropriate option to fill in the blank labelled as (2)?", "o": ["consideration", "exaggeration", "proliferation", "extravagance 5. flamboyance"], "a": 0}, {"n": 20, "q": "Which of the following is the most appropriate option to fill in the blank labelled as (3)?", "o": ["resilient", "innate", "enigmatic", "ineffable 5. invasive"], "a": 1}, {"n": 21, "q": "Which of the following is the most appropriate option to fill in the blank labelled as (4)?", "o": ["aversion", "harmony", "virtue", "apathy 5. deception"], "a": 2}, {"n": 22, "q": "Which of the following is the most appropriate option to fill in the blank labelled as (5)?", "o": [". intricacy", ". ambiguity", ". animosity", ". tenacity 5. sympathy"], "a": 4}, {"n": 23, "q": "Which of the following is the most appropriate option to fill in the blank labelled as (6)?", "o": [". engrossed", ". averted", ". pondered", ". focused 5. flinched"], "a": 1}, {"n": 24, "q": "Which of the phrases given below the sentence should replace the word/phrase that is underlined in the sentence to make it grammatically correct? If the sentence is correct as it is given and no correction is required, mark 'No correction required' as the answer. He is one of those players who has won many accolades in such a short time.", "o": [". one of those players who have", ". one of those player who have", ". one of those player who has", ". one off those players who have 5. no correction required"], "a": 0}, {"n": 25, "q": "Which of the phrases given below the sentence should replace the word/phrase that is underlined in the sentence to make it grammatically correct? If the sentence is correct as it is given and no correction is required, mark 'No correction required' as the answer. The doleful news of the boy dying from malaria brought about an envelope of gloom in the locality.", "o": [". dying off", ". die from", ". die of", ". dying of 5. no correction required"], "a": 3}, {"n": 26, "q": "Which of the phrases given below the sentence should replace the word/phrase that is underlined to make it grammatically correct? If the sentence is correct as it is given and no correction is required, mark 'No correction required' as the answer. I am certain that Subham would've lent you money if you would've asked him.", "o": [". should've", ". had asked him.", ". will have asked him", ". will have been asking him 5. No correction required"], "a": 1}, {"n": 27, "q": "Direction- A part of the sentence is underlined. Below are given five alternatives which may improve the word. Choose the correct alternative. I will have wrote articles on different topics before you come.", "o": [". will have writing", ". will have been write", ". will have written", ". will have writes 5. will have been written"], "a": 2}, {"n": 28, "q": "A sentence/ a part of a sentence is underlined. Four alternatives are given to the underlined part which will improve the meaning of the sentence. Choose the correct alternatives. In case no improvement needed, click the option corresponding to 'No improvement'. India is a country of rich culture and has century of history and tradition of its own.", "o": [". centuries of histories", ". centuries of history", ". century of histories", ". century from history 5. No improvement"], "a": 1}, {"n": 29, "q": "Rearrange the following six sentences/ group of sentences (A), (B), (C), (D), (E) and (F) in the proper sequence to form a meaningful paragraph; then answer the questions given below them: A. By having launched schemes for girl child education, we come close to achieving our aims of equal society. B. But, there are several hurdles on the road of establishing women empowerment schemes through government policies. C. Women empowerment is one of the most important elements for equality. D. Many have considered it to be the backbone to create a society free from gender bias. E. However, the efforts are constant in the direction to achieve the goals. F. This will create equal opportunities for women and will empower women from an early age. What will be the first sentence after rearrangement?", "o": [". A", ". C", ". F", ". E 5. B"], "a": 1}, {"n": 30, "q": "What will be the third sentence after rearrangement?", "o": [". B", ". F", ". E", ". D 5. A"], "a": 0}, {"n": 31, "q": "What will be the fourth sentence after rearrangement?", "o": [". C", ". A", ". F", ". E 5. D"], "a": 3}, {"n": 32, "q": "What will be the last sentence after rearrangement?", "o": [". D", ". E", ". F", ". A 5. B"], "a": 2}, {"n": 33, "q": "What will be the Second sentence after rearrangement?", "o": [". D", ". C", ". F", ". E 5. B"], "a": 0}, {"n": 34, "q": "A sentence is given with three words marked as (A), (B), and (C). These words may or may not be placed in their places. Four options with different arrangements of these words are given. Mark the option with the correct arrangement as the answer. If there is no change required, mark 'No rearrangement required' as your answer. The most economic (A) determinant of important (B) buoyancy in India is private (C) investment.", "o": [". ACB", ". BAC", ". BCA", ". CBA 5. No rearrangement required"], "a": 1}, {"n": 35, "q": "A sentence is given with three words marked as (A), (B), and (C). These words may or may not be placed in their places. Four options with different arrangements of these words are given. Mark the option with the correct arrangement as the answer. If there is no change required, mark 'No rearrangement required' as your answer. The Niti Aayog has measures (A) all states to take urged (B) to reduce(C) the logistics cost of business.", "o": [". CAB", ". BCA", ". ACB", ". BAC 5. No rearrangement required"], "a": 3}, {"n": 36, "q": "A sentence is given with three words marked as (A), (B), and (C). These words may or may not be placed in their places. Four options with different arrangements of these words are given. Mark the option with the correct arrangement as the answer. If there is no change required, mark 'No rearrangement required' as your answer. India has a plan to ambitious (A) about 450 gigawatts of produce (B) power by 2030; it’s a very renewable(C) goal.", "o": ["BCA", "BAC", "CAB", "CBA 5. No rearrangement required"], "a": 0}, {"n": 37, "q": "Directions: The following question has two blanks, each blank indicating that something has been omitted. Choose the set of words for each blank that best fits in the context of the sentence. The automobile dealerships are among the worst _______ segments within the _______ automotive value chain, ICRA said in a statement.", "o": [". impacting, entiring", ". impact, entire", ". impacts, entered", ". impacted, enter 5. impacted, entire"], "a": 4}, {"n": 38, "q": "Directions: The following question has two blanks, each blank indicating that something has been omitted. Choose the set of words for each blank that best fits in the context of the sentence. Besides, the _______ specification for food-grains has been _______ for paddy procurement.", "o": [". uniform, issued", ". uniformly, issued", ". uniform, issue", ". uniformity, issues 5. uniformed, issue"], "a": 0}, {"n": 39, "q": "Directions: The following question has two blanks, each blank indicating that something has been omitted. Choose the set of words for each blank that best fits in the context of the sentence. India’s shrinking economy is not _______ foreign investors from pouring money into the nation’s _______ betting on a recovery.", "o": [". stopped, stock", ". stopping, stocked", ". stops, stocking", ". stopping, stock 5. stop, stocker"], "a": 3}, {"n": 40, "q": "Directions: Given below is a sentence containing an underlined idiom. You have to determine whether the idiom is best suited for the sentence or not. If not, choose the correct idiom from the given options that fits the sentence most appropriately. After years of contemplation, she decided to break the ice and quit her stable job to pursue her dream of becoming an artist.", "o": [". Kick the bucket", ". Cross the Rubicon", ". Burn the midnight oil", ". Spill the beans 5. No change is required"], "a": 1}, {"n": 41, "q": "Directions: Read the data carefully and answer the following questions. The following table shows the number of public sector employees living in a building, the ratio of public to private sector employees, and the percentage of vacant flats in the building. Building Public Sector Employees Ratio (Public : Private) % of Vacant Flats A 120 3:2 20% B a 3:5 20% C 90 2:3 25% D 2a 5:4 55% Note: 1) The total number of flats in each building is equal to the sum of public sector employees, private sector employees, and vacant flats. 2) The total number of public sector employees in all buildings together is 300. If 40% of the private sector employees in Building C move to Building D, and 25% of the public sector employees in Building A move to Building B, what is the new ratio of total occupied flats in Building C to the total occupied flats in Building D?", "o": ["11:7", "13:9", "15:11", "17:13 5. 19:18"], "a": 4}, {"n": 42, "q": "If the average rent per occupied flat in Building B is ₹12,000 and the average rent per occupied flat in Building D is ₹18,000, what is the difference between the total rent collected from Building B and Building D?", "o": ["₹ 5,68,000", "₹ 6,82,000", "₹ 8,55,000", "₹ 9,84,000 5. None of these"], "a": 3}, {"n": 43, "q": "If the ratio of male to female public sector employees in Building A is 5:3 and in Building C it is 4:5, what percentage of the total public sector employees in Buildings A and C together are female?", "o": ["45.24%", "51.25%", "53.76%", "56.25% 5. 48.75%"], "a": 0}, {"n": 44, "q": "If 75% of the vacant flats in Building D are converted into community halls and 33.33% of the remaining vacant flats are then converted into small offices, how many flats remain vacant in Building D?", "o": ["14", "15", "26", "17 5. 22"], "a": 4}, {"n": 45, "q": "If the number of private sector employees in Building B increases by 40% and the number of public sector employees in Building D decreases by 25%, what is the new ratio of private sector employees in Building B to public sector employees in Building D?", "o": ["8:5", "14:9", "10:3", "11:6 5. 9:4"], "a": 1}, {"n": 46, "q": "If a new building (E) is constructed with the same total number of flats as Buildings B and C combined, and the percentage of vacant flats in Building E is the average of the percentages in Buildings B and D, how many vacant flats will Building E have?", "o": ["140", "150", "200", "230 5. 55"], "a": 1}, {"n": 47, "q": "The ratio of previous and current salary of each employee of company A is 3 : 4 respectively while the ratio of number of previous employees and current is 5 : 3 respectively, then company A had a profit of Rs 90000. Find the previous expenditure of company A on the salary of employees.", "o": ["225000", "450000", "405000", "360000 5. 550000"], "a": 1}, {"n": 48, "q": "In a mixture (milk + water) of 200 lit, ratio of quantity of milk and water is 12:13, respectively. If x lit of the mixture is replaced with same quantity of water, then the ratio of quantity of milk to that of water in the resultant becomes 9:16. Find the value of x.", "o": ["40", "50", "65", "60 5. 55"], "a": 1}, {"n": 49, "q": "A, B and C started business with Rs. (x - 2500) , Rs.(x + 2000) and Rs. (x + 6500) respectively. Investment time is equal for all three. The ratio between the investment of A and C is 35: 53 respectively. If the difference between profit share A and C is Rs. 3600. Find the profit share of B.", "o": ["Rs. 9600", "Rs. 7800", "Rs. 8800", "Rs. 6600 5. Rs. 8400"], "a": 2}, {"n": 50, "q": "A and B together to fill the whole tank in 20/3 min. The efficiency ratio of A and B is 5: 4. B and C together can fill the same tank in 60/7 min. If A and C together opened for 6 minutes and the remaining x% of the tank is to be filled by C. Find the value of x.", "o": ["30%", "15%", "20%", "25% 5. 10%"], "a": 2}, {"n": 51, "q": "There are 300 students in a college, each participating in different sports: chess, cricket, and volleyball. The number of students who play only chess is twice the number of students who play only chess and volleyball. The number of students who play only chess and volleyball is 20% less than the number of students who play only chess and cricket. 10% of the total students play all three sports, and this number is exactly half of the number of students who play only cricket. The number of students who play only volleyball is equal to the number of students who play only cricket and volleyball. The number of students who play only volleyball and the number of students who play only cricket and volleyball both is the same, which is 2/30 of the total student population. Find Students playing only cricket is what percent more/less than the students playing only cricket and chess together.", "o": ["20%", "25%", "15%", "12% 5. 18%"], "a": 0}, {"n": 52, "q": "Find the average number of students playing only one game.", "o": ["52", "53", "53.33", "54.2 5. 48.25"], "a": 2}, {"n": 53, "q": "Find the number of students playing at least 2 games.", "o": ["120", "110", "140", "150 5. 70"], "a": 2}, {"n": 54, "q": "Find the Ratio of students playing only chess and only cricket together to the students playing all of the 3 sports.", "o": ["12 : 7", "14 : 15", "14 : 3", "4:7 5. 6 : 11"], "a": 2}, {"n": 55, "q": "If 25% of the students playing only chess started playing all 3 types of sports, then how many students play all 3 types of sports?", "o": ["60", "70", "50", "35 5. 55"], "a": 2}, {"n": 56, "q": "Find the wrong term in the following series. 16, 67, 244, 663, 1000,787", "o": ["1000", "787", "663", "244 5. 67"], "a": 0}, {"n": 57, "q": "Find the wrong term in the following series. 247, 249, 501, 1507, 6055, 30171", "o": ["247", "249", "501", "6055 5. 30171"], "a": 3}, {"n": 58, "q": "Given that the simple interest accrued from a sum of Rs. 2800 at an annual rate of 10% over 3 years is Rs. x and Rs. 1736 is the simple interest gained from an investment of Rs. 6200 at a 14% annual rate over a period of y years, can you determine the value of x/y?", "o": ["550", "380", "420", "140 5. 240"], "a": 2}, {"n": 59, "q": "There are 4 consecutive odd numbers, x1 , x2 , x3 and x4 and three consecutive even numbers y1 , y2 and y3 . The average of the odd numbers is 6 less than the average of the even numbers. If the sum of the three even numbers is 16 less than the sum of the four odd numbers, what is the average of x1 , x2, x3 and x4?", "o": ["30", "35", "38", "32 5. 34"], "a": 4}, {"n": 60, "q": "Cost price of an article is Rs. (x + 150). If it is marked up by 30% above its cost price and sold at the two consecutive discounts of 10% and 20% respectively. After the two successive discounts the article is sold at Rs. 842.4. Find the value of x", "o": ["720", "650", "750", "700 5. 600"], "a": 2}, {"n": 61, "q": "The average speed of the boat is 9.1 km/hr. The ratio between the speed of the stream and the upstream speed of the boat is 3: 7. The sum of the time taken by the boat to travel (D + 23) km downstream and (1.2D - 27) km upstream is 60 hours. Find the time taken by the boat to cover D km in still water", "o": ["32 hours", "25 hours", "20 hours", "16 hours 5. 36 hours"], "a": 1}, {"n": 62, "q": "If the length and breadth of the rectangle are l cm and b cm respectively.The area of the rectangle and the perimeter of the rectangle are 192 m² and 56 m, respectively. If the radius of the circle is 2 less than the length of the rectangle, then find the area of the circle.", "o": ["320", "510", "616", "436 5. 210"], "a": 2}, {"n": 63, "q": "Directions: Read the data carefully and answer the following questions. The bar graph shows the total number of newspapers and magazines sold by five organizations (A, B, C, D, E). The pie chart shows the percentage of newspapers sold by each organization. Note: The total number of newspapers sold by E is 960. Determine the difference between x% of the number of Magazines sold by D and y% of the number of Newspapers sold by C if the number of Magazines by A is x% of the total number of Newspapers and magazines sold by A and the number of Newspapers sold by D is y% of the number of Newspapers sold by C.", "o": ["268", "372", "354", "112 5. None of these"], "a": 2}, {"n": 64, "q": "Determine the ratio between the number of Religious Books Sold by B and the number of Newspapers in sold by A if the number of Books sold by B is equal to the average number of Magazines sold by C, D, and E and the ratio of Horror, Comedy, and Religious Books sold by B is 5:3:2.", "o": ["71:73", "62:81", "79:77", "56:57 5. None of these"], "a": 2}, {"n": 65, "q": "If organization E increases its newspaper sales by 15% and decreases its magazine sales by 20%, while organization B increases its magazine sales by 25% and decreases its newspaper sales by 10%, what is the percentage difference between the new total number of newspapers sold by E and the new total number of magazines sold by B (rounded to two decimal places)?", "o": ["2.35%", "5.97%", "6.22%", "8.55% 5. 4.78%"], "a": 1}, {"n": 66, "q": "If organizations A and C decide to merge and sell their combined newspapers and magazines at a uniform price of ₹20 per item, while organizations B and D decide to sell their combined newspapers and magazines at a uniform price of ₹22 per item, what is the difference between the total revenue generated by the merged organizations (A+C) and the merged organizations (B+D)?", "o": ["₹30,220", "₹32,480", "₹24,630", "₹27,810 5. ₹29,840"], "a": 4}, {"n": 67, "q": "Determine the number of Magazines sold by J, if the number of Magazines cars sold by J is 25% more than (P + a + 20), where P is the number of Newspapers sold by E.", "o": ["2010", "1350", "1680", "1540 5. 1275"], "a": 4}, {"n": 68, "q": "In a class consists of x person and their average weight is 48. If the person whose weight is 68 kg is replaced by a person whose weight is 72 kg then the average increases by 0.25. If the value of x is increased by 25% and the average weight of the persons decreased by 50%. Find the new total weight.", "o": ["780 kg", "480 kg", "720 kg", "640 kg 5. 840 kg"], "a": 1}, {"n": 69, "q": "The present age of the father is 54 years and the present age of the son is 1/6th of the present age of the father. If x years ago, the age of the father to son is in the ratio 10: 1. The present age of the mother is (8x + 4) . Find the ratio between the present age of mother and father.", "o": ["4:3", "2:3", "3:2", "2:1 5. 4:5"], "a": 1}, {"n": 70, "q": "The salary of Arun and Arul is Rs. x and Rs. y respectively and the salary of arun is 66.66% of the total salary of Arun and Arul. Salary of Arul is 50% of the salary of Arun. If the difference between the salary of Arun and Arul is Rs. 4000. Find the value of 140% of y?", "o": ["Rs. 4800", "Rs. 4400", "Rs. 5600", "Rs. 4200 5. Rs. 5400"], "a": 2}, {"n": 71, "q": "Direction: Read the following information carefully and answer the question that follow. Nine boxes O, P, Q, R, S, T, U, V and W are kept one above another not necessarily in the same order. Bottom box is numbered as 1 and top box is numbered as 9. Four boxes are placed between T and U. More than Four boxes are placed above the box U, which is even number box. Two boxes are placed between box O and P, which is placed just above box U. There are three boxes are placed between box S and box R, which is placed just above box T. More than three boxes are placed between box P and box V, which is placed above box O. More than two boxes are placed between box W and box Q, which is not placed above box P. How many boxes between the box R and P?", "o": ["One", "Two", "Three", "Four 5. None of these"], "a": 3}, {"n": 72, "q": "Which among the following is 6th number box?", "o": [". S", ". W", ". O", ". V 5. Q"], "a": 2}, {"n": 73, "q": "How many boxes are above the box U?", "o": [". Six", ". Nine", ". Eight", ". Seven 5. None of these"], "a": 3}, {"n": 74, "q": "If R is related to V and O is related to T in certain way, then Q is related to?", "o": [". S", ". U", ". O", ". V 5. Q"], "a": 1}, {"n": 75, "q": "Which is the box placed at the bottom?", "o": [". S", ". W", ". O", ". V 5. Q"], "a": 4}, {"n": 76, "q": "Direction : Read the following information carefully and answer the questions based on given information. Nine persons D, G, J, M, O, P, T, V, Y works in a company at different designations ,i.e., CEO, COO , CFO, CTO, CMO, CSO, VP, GM, Director from higher to lower positions such that CEO is at the highest position and Director is at lowest position. Only two designations are there between M and G. As many persons senior to T as many persons junior to him. D is neither GM nor COO. Less than four persons have their designation between T and D. J and V either immediately senior or immediately junior to M. Only three persons are senior to V. As many people senior to J as many are junior to Y. D is not immediately senior or junior to T. P is senior to G. Less than two post between T and O. Which of the following is correctly matced ?", "o": [". P - CFO", ". M - CTO", ". T - CMO", ". O - VP 5. Both"], "a": 4}, {"n": 77, "q": "Find odd one out.", "o": [". TM", ". GY", ". OV", ". OD 5. PM"], "a": 2}, {"n": 78, "q": "Which of the following statements is true ?", "o": [". P is senior most person.", ". G is CFO.", ". D is not the last person.", ". Only two people are designated between T and O. 5. None of these"], "a": 0}, {"n": 79, "q": "How many people are designated between V and D ?", "o": [". Two", ". Three", ". One", ". Four 5. None"], "a": 3}, {"n": 80, "q": "Who among them is CSO ?", "o": [". P", ". V", ". T", ". Y 5. None of these"], "a": 4}, {"n": 81, "q": "Direction: In the question below are given three statements followed by three conclusions I, II, and III. You have to take the given statements to be true even if they seem to be at variance from commonly known facts, Read all the given conclusions and then decide which of the following conclusions logically follows from the given statements disregarding commonly known facts. Statements: Only a few Mobile are Charger. All Charger are Black. Only a few Black are White. Conclusions: I. Some White being Charger is a possibility. II. Some Mobile being Black is a possibility. III. Some Black are not White is a possibility.", "o": [". Only Conclusion I follows", ". Only Conclusion II follows", ". Only Conclusion III follows", ". Both Conclusion I and III follows 5. All Conclusion follows"], "a": 0}, {"n": 82, "q": "Direction: In the question below are given four statements followed by four conclusions numbered I, II, III and IV. You have to take the given statements to be true even if they seem to be at variance with commonly known facts. Read all the conclusions and then decide which of the given conclusions logically follows from the given statements disregarding commonly known facts. Statements: I. All James are Holmes. II. No Sherlock is Mycroft. III. All Sherlock is James. IV. No James is Watson. Conclusions: I. Some Mycroft are James. II. All Holmes being Watson is a possibility. III. No Mycroft is James.", "o": [". Both I and II follows", ". All except III follows", ". All except II follows", ". Either I or III follows 5. None of these"], "a": 3}, {"n": 83, "q": "Directions: In the question below are given three statements followed by three conclusions. You have to take the given statements to be true even if they seem to be at variance with commonly known facts. Read all the conclusions and then decide which of the given conclusions logically follows from the given statements disregarding commonly known facts. Statements: Only a few Pens are Pencils Some Pencils are Rubber Only a few Rubber are Sharpener Conclusions: I. Some Pencil are not Rubber II. All Pencil are Rubber III. Some Pens being Sharpener is a possibility", "o": [". Only I follow", ". Only II and III follow", ". Only III follow", ". Either I or II follow and III follow 5. None follow"], "a": 3}, {"n": 84, "q": "Directions: Read the following information carefully and answer the questions based on given information. There are fourteen persons sitting in two parallel rows such that seven persons sits on each row. In row 1 persons such that A to G sits and faces towards south direction and in row 2 persons such that P to V sits and faces towards north direction but not necessarily in same order. B sits second to the right of the person who sits opposite to Q. C is the only neighbor of F. As many people sits to the right of D as many to the left of A. P sits opposite to the one who sits immediate right of F. Only two persons sit between U and S. Less than three persons sits to the left of A. Only three people sit S and T, who sits at one of the extreme end. D is not facing Q. R is not sitting at any extreme end. There are two person between G and E where E is not on extreme end. Which of the following is incorrectly matched ?", "o": ["B-U", "D-R", "A-S", "G-T 5. C-V"], "a": 4}, {"n": 85, "q": "Find the odd one out.", "o": [". G", ". F", ". R", ". T 5. V"], "a": 2}, {"n": 86, "q": "Which of the following statement(s) is / are true ? A) G sits second to the left of D. B) Only two person sits between R and T. C) E sits opposite to Q.", "o": [". Only A", ". Only B", ". Both A and B", ". Neither A nor B 5. Only C"], "a": 4}, {"n": 87, "q": "Who sits opposite to the person who sits immediate left of C ?", "o": [". P", ". S", ". U", ". V 5. None of these"], "a": 3}, {"n": 88, "q": "Who among sits at extreme end ?", "o": [". G and F", ". B and C", ". U and V", ". T and V 5. Both option"], "a": 4}, {"n": 89, "q": "How many such pair of digits are there in the number '1537862', each of which has as many digits between them in the number (both forward and backward direction) as they have between them in the general numerical order?", "o": ["Two", "Four", "Five", "One 5. Six"], "a": 4}, {"n": 90, "q": "Direction: Read the following information carefully and answer the questions based on given information. Nine persons E, G, I, J, R, T, Y, M, N studies in three different university which are Cambridge University, Trinity University, O×ford University and likes nine different colours that are White, Green, Yellow, Pink, Red, Violet, Orange, Black, Grey but not necessarily in the same order. Not less than two person and more than four person studies in the same university. T studies in the same university in which the person who likes Red colour studies. R and G likes orange and white but not necessarily in same order. The person who likes Pink colour studies in the same university in which I studies. R and E studies in different university but not in Trinity University. Neither M nor N likes Green or Red. R and Y likes Red and Orange but not necessarily in the same order. J doesn’t study in O×ford University, studies with the person who likes orange colour. G studies in Trinity University with the person who like violet colour. T and I likes violet and yellow but not necessarily in same order. N studies in with person who likes Red colour. N likes Black colour. Persons who studies in Trinity University is one more than the persons who studies in O×ford University. I is not studying in Trinity University. Cambridge has least number of person among the three. E likes pink colour. Which of the following pair is incorrect?", "o": [". J - White", ". R - Orange", ". E - Pink", ". T - Violet 5. None of these"], "a": 0}, {"n": 91, "q": "Which of the following statement is / are correct ? A) G and T studies in same college. B) Y likes Red colour. C) J likes Green colour.", "o": [". Only A", ". Only B", ". Only C", ". Both A and C 5. All of these"], "a": 4}, {"n": 92, "q": "Which of the following statement is are true ?", "o": [". J studies in Trinity University.", ". R studies with G.", ". I studies in Trinity University", ". R studies in Oxford University 5. Y studies with T in Trinity University."], "a": 4}, {"n": 93, "q": "Who among them studies in same college as of I ?", "o": [". Y", ". T", ". E", ". R 5. J"], "a": 2}, {"n": 94, "q": "Who among them likes green colour ?", "o": [". J", ". Y", ". E", ". I 5. G"], "a": 0}, {"n": 95, "q": "Five letter-clusters have been given, out of which four are alike in some manner and one is different. Select the letter-cluster that is different.", "o": [". CFIL", ". MPSV", ". DGJM", ". SPMJ 5. KNQT"], "a": 3}, {"n": 96, "q": "Direction: Study the following information carefully to answer the questions given below- Seven persons A, D, G, O, P, S and T lives on seven floor building. Each person lives on each floor and no floor is vacant. Each of them likes different flower Lily, Rose, Tulip, Iris, Sunflower, Marigold, Orchid, but not necessarily in same order. The ground floor is numbered as floor", "o": ["and above floor is numbered as floor", "and so on and the top floor is numbered as floor 7. D and A are not like Iris and none of them lives on 6th floor. O likes Iris and neither lives on", "rd floor nor 7th floor. T lives exactly between D and S. A likes Lily and lives on", "th floor. The one who likes Orchid lives between the one who likes Marigold and Sunflower. P likes Rose and lives on 6th floor. G lives above of O. The one likes Marigold lives on"], "a": 3}, {"n": 97, "q": "Which of the following pair is not correct?", "o": [". P - Rose", ". A - Lily", ". D - Marigold", ". T - Orchid 5. S - Iris"], "a": 4}, {"n": 98, "q": "How many persons are living between D and G?", "o": [". One", ". Two", ". Three", ". Four 5. None"], "a": 2}, {"n": 99, "q": "The person who is on 7th floor likes which flower?", "o": [". Orchid", ". Iris", ". Tulip", ". Marigold 5. Rose"], "a": 2}, {"n": 100, "q": "Who of the following lives in 2nd floor?", "o": ["P", "T", "S", "A 5. G"], "a": 1}]});

